{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wr6LYi1vYwpjnSXUGyANZS","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Discovery + principled negative result + practical recommendation\n2\t  三段叙事。 (1) Pareto frontier 在 Qwen3-235B 上清晰（rho ~ -0.50），在 Llama 4 Scout 上 language-specific（global\n3\t  rho ~ -0.12）：部分语言随 depth 改善（ar/ko/hi）， 部分退化（zh/sw），验证 architecture-dependent tradeoff\n4\t  shape。 (2) CaCLR β sweep 3 OOM 证明 MMD consistency loss inert（d=0.07, p=0.38）。 CKA\n5\t  几何分析提供 suggestive 解释——MMD matches marginals but not low-dim directional structure——但\n6\t  partial correlation controlling depth 仅 r=0.18, p=0.11，降级为 suggestive correlational\n7\t  analysis。Between-language correlation 成立（same-layer r=0.52, p<0.01）。 (3) Linear\n8\t  projection ~50 pairs 是实际方案（+3.5pp over zero-shot），surpasses CaCLR at ~20 pairs。\n9\t  Decomposition 定性成立（65% combos improved, d=0.25），orthogonality 跨语言持续 但 low-resource\n10\t  variance 增大（cosine max 0.11）。 Control task artifact warning 升级为独立贡献：~27% lang-layer\n11\t  combos selectivity < 0.05，集中在 low-resource + shallow layers。 Target: EACL borderline\n12\t  accept，以 discovery + systematic negative result 发表。\n13\t\n14\t  '\n15\timagined_experiments:\n16\t- name: Qwen3-235B-A22B Full Pareto Frontier\n17\t  plan_id: plan_001\n18\t  description: 'Full Pareto frontier on Qwen3-235B-A22B (94 layers, MoE, INT4): 24\n19\t    probed layers (every 4th), 20 languages, EN correctness probes (LogReg + MLP),\n20\t    5 transfer conditions. Per-language Spearman rho.\n21\t\n22\t    '\n23\t  expected_results:\n24\t    en_best_auroc: 0.8\n25\t    en_best_layer: 72\n26\t    en_best_ece_raw: 0.175\n27\t    en_auroc_range:\n28\t    - 0.54\n29\t    - 0.8\n30\t    en_auroc_at_50pct_depth_L48: 0.77\n31\t    en_auroc_profile_summary: 'L0-L20: 0.54-0.67 (early buildup); L24-L44: 0.70-0.76\n32\t      (mid layers); L48-L68: 0.77-0.80 (approaching peak); L72: 0.80 (peak); L76-L92:\n33\t      0.79-0.75 (slight decline)\n34\t\n35\t      '\n36\t    zs_at_en_optimal_L72:\n37\t      zh: 0.71\n38\t      es: 0.7\n39\t      fr: 0.7\n40\t      de: 0.69\n41\t      ja: 0.67\n42\t      pt: 0.69\n43\t      nl: 0.68\n44\t      ru: 0.67\n45\t      ar: 0.65\n46\t      hi: 0.64\n47\t      ko: 0.66\n48\t      vi: 0.64\n49\t      tr: 0.63\n50\t      id: 0.65\n51\t      pl: 0.66\n52\t      uk: 0.65\n53\t      sw: 0.55\n54\t      bn: 0.54\n55\t      te: 0.56\n56\t      avg: 0.647\n57\t    zs_at_best_transfer_L48:\n58\t      zh: 0.73\n59\t      es: 0.72\n60\t      fr: 0.71\n61\t      de: 0.7\n62\t      ja: 0.69\n63\t      pt: 0.7\n64\t      nl: 0.69\n65\t      ru: 0.69\n66\t      ar: 0.67\n67\t      hi: 0.66\n68\t      ko: 0.68\n69\t      vi: 0.66\n70\t      tr: 0.65\n71\t      id: 0.67\n72\t      pl: 0.68\n73\t      uk: 0.67\n74\t      sw: 0.58\n75\t      bn: 0.57\n76\t      te: 0.59\n77\t      avg: 0.669\n78\t    pareto_rho_global: -0.5\n79\t    pareto_rho_per_lang_median: -0.48\n80\t    pareto_rho_per_lang:\n81\t      zh: -0.45\n82\t      es: -0.42\n83\t      fr: -0.43\n84\t      de: -0.44\n85\t      ja: -0.47\n86\t      pt: -0.43\n87\t      nl: -0.44\n88\t      ru: -0.46\n89\t      ar: -0.5\n90\t      hi: -0.52\n91\t      ko: -0.48\n92\t      vi: -0.51\n93\t      tr: -0.53\n94\t      id: -0.49\n95\t      pl: -0.46\n96\t      uk: -0.47\n97\t      sw: -0.58\n98\t      bn: -0.56\n99\t      te: -0.55\n100\t    pareto_rho_range:\n101\t    - -0.58\n102\t    - -0.42\n103\t    zs_langs_above_060: 16\n104\t    zs_langs_above_065: 13\n105\t    transfer_methods_at_L48:\n106\t      zero_shot_avg: 0.669\n107\t      mean_shift_avg: 0.669\n108\t      mean_shift_delta: 0.0\n109\t      linear_proj_50_avg: 0.704\n110\t      linear_proj_50_delta: 0.035\n111\t      fewshot_25_avg: 0.695\n112\t      fewshot_25_delta: 0.026\n113\t      fewshot_100_avg: 0.715\n114\t      fewshot_100_delta: 0.046\n115\t      caclr_best_avg: 0.677\n116\t      caclr_best_delta: 0.008\n117\t    bootstrap_ci_linear_proj_delta:\n118\t    - 0.025\n119\t    - 0.045\n120\t    bootstrap_ci_fewshot100_delta:\n121\t    - 0.035\n122\t    - 0.057\n123\t    bootstrap_ci_caclr_delta:\n124\t    - -0.003\n125\t    - 0.019\n126\t  result_rationale: 'Qwen3-235B-A22B 是 94 层 MoE 架构，显著深于 MVP 的 7B 模型。EN best AUROC\n127\t    从 MVP 的 0.754 提升到 0.80，因为更大模型编码更强的 correctness signal。 Peak 在 ~77% depth (L72)，与\n128\t    MVP pattern 一致——correctness 在 deep-but-not-final 层达到峰值。\n129\t\n130\t    Pareto frontier 清晰（median per-lang rho = -0.48）因为：(a) 94 层提供足够 depth gradient\n131\t    让 language specialization 逐渐显现；(b) 所有 20 语言在更深层 的 transfer 都退化，只是退化速度不同。Low-resource\n132\t    语言（sw/bn/te）rho 更强 负（-0.55 ~ -0.58）因为它们的跨语言表征从一开始就弱，depth-induced specialization\n133\t    影响更大。High-resource 语言 rho 较温和（-0.42 ~ -0.45）因为 丰富的预训练数据使深层仍保持合理的跨语言对齐。\n134\t\n135\t    Best transfer layer (L48, ~51% depth) vs EN-optimal (L72, ~77% depth) 的 gap 是\n136\t    Pareto tradeoff 的直接体现：L48 平均 ZS AUROC 0.669 vs L72 的 0.647， 差 2.2pp。\n137\t\n138\t    Mean-shift ΔAUROC ≡ 0 符合数学证明（rank-invariance under StandardScaler + logistic regression）。Linear\n139\t    projection +3.5pp 因为直接学习 rotation correction。CaCLR +0.8pp 几乎全来自 α (SB-ECE) 项而非\n140\t    β (MMD) 项。\n141\t\n142\t    '\n143\t  tables:\n144\t  - name: 'Table 1: Qwen3-235B Zero-Shot Transfer AUROC (Language × Layer)'\n145\t    description: '24 probed layers (rows) × 20 languages + EN (columns)。 Cells: AUROC。Bold:\n146\t      per-language best layer。Gray: within 1pp of best。 Bottom: per-language Spearman\n147\t      rho ± bootstrap 95% CI。 Key pattern: EN-optimal L72 ≠ transfer-optimal L48 for\n148\t      all languages。 Resource-tier banding visible: HIGH langs (zh/es/fr/de) show\n149\t      flatter profiles; LOW langs (sw/bn/te) show steeper drop-off at deep layers。\n150\t\n151\t      '\n152\t  - name: 'Table 2: Qwen3-235B Transfer Method Comparison'\n153\t    description: '5 methods (columns) × 20 langs (rows), at two fixed layers (L48\n154\t      = 50% depth, L72 = EN-optimal) + per-lang oracle。AUROC, ΔAUROC vs zero-shot,\n155\t      bootstrap 95% CI, paired permutation p, Cohen''s d。\n156\t\n157\t      '\n158\t  figures_description:\n159\t  - 'Pareto frontier scatter: x = EN AUROC (per layer), y = median ZS transfer AUROC\n160\t    (20 langs)。Each point = one layer, annotated with layer number。 Pareto-optimal\n161\t    frontier highlighted。Separate traces for HIGH/MID/LOW resource tiers showing tier-dependent\n162\t    frontier shape。Clear tradeoff visible。\n163\t\n164\t    '\n165\t  - 'Per-language Spearman rho bar chart: 20 bars sorted by |rho|, color by resource\n166\t    tier。Error bars = bootstrap 95% CI。All bars negative, clustered between -0.42\n167\t    and -0.58。Horizontal reference at rho = 0 for contrast with Llama 4 Scout (plan_002)\n168\t    where some bars cross zero。\n169\t\n170\t    '\n171\t  analysis: 'Qwen3-235B 作为 \"strong Pareto architecture\" 的角色得到验证：所有 20 语言 都展现一致的 depth-transfer\n172\t    tradeoff（全部 rho 负值），没有例外。 Architecture-specific 特征是 MoE routing 引入的层间异质性使 frontier\n173\t    不如 dense model 平滑（per-layer variance 较高），但总趋势清晰。 16/20 语言在最优 transfer layer 达到\n174\t    >0.60 AUROC，13/20 达到 >0.65， 验证 zero-shot probe transfer 对 majority languages 可行。\n175\t    sw/bn/te 的失败是 pretraining representation 的基础限制，非 architecture-specific。\n176\t\n177\t    '\n178\t- name: Llama 4 Scout Full Pareto Frontier\n179\t  plan_id: plan_002\n180\t  description: 'Full Pareto frontier on Llama 4 Scout (48 layers, MoE, W4A16): 12\n181\t    probed layers (every 4th), 20 languages, 5 transfer conditions. Per-language Spearman\n182\t    rho. Architecture contrast with Qwen3-235B.\n183\t\n184\t    '\n185\t  expected_results:\n186\t    en_best_auroc: 0.78\n187\t    en_best_layer: 40\n188\t    en_best_ece_raw: 0.185\n189\t    en_auroc_range:\n190\t    - 0.55\n191\t    - 0.78\n192\t    en_auroc_at_50pct_depth_L24: 0.73\n193\t    zs_at_en_optimal_L40:\n194\t      zh: 0.67\n195\t      es: 0.66\n196\t      fr: 0.66\n197\t      de: 0.65\n198\t      ja: 0.64\n199\t      pt: 0.65\n200\t      nl: 0.64\n201\t      ru: 0.64\n202\t      ar: 0.65\n203\t      hi: 0.63\n204\t      ko: 0.66\n205\t      vi: 0.62\n206\t      tr: 0.61\n207\t      id: 0.63\n208\t      pl: 0.64\n209\t      uk: 0.63\n210\t      sw: 0.54\n211\t      bn: 0.53\n212\t      te: 0.55\n213\t      avg: 0.627\n214\t    zs_at_per_lang_best:\n215\t      zh:\n216\t        auroc: 0.69\n217\t        best_layer: 24\n218\t      es:\n219\t        auroc: 0.68\n220\t        best_layer: 24\n221\t      fr:\n222\t        auroc: 0.68\n223\t        best_layer: 28\n224\t      de:\n225\t        auroc: 0.67\n226\t        best_layer: 24\n227\t      ja:\n228\t        auroc: 0.66\n229\t        best_layer: 28\n230\t      pt:\n231\t        auroc: 0.67\n232\t        best_layer: 24\n233\t      nl:\n234\t        auroc: 0.66\n235\t        best_layer: 28\n236\t      ru:\n237\t        auroc: 0.66\n238\t        best_layer: 28\n239\t      ar:\n240\t        auroc: 0.66\n241\t        best_layer: 40\n242\t      hi:\n243\t        auroc: 0.64\n244\t        best_layer: 36\n245\t      ko:\n246\t        auroc: 0.67\n247\t        best_layer: 40\n248\t      vi:\n249\t        auroc: 0.64\n250\t        best_layer: 32\n251\t      tr:\n252\t        auroc: 0.63\n253\t        best_layer: 32\n254\t      id:\n255\t        auroc: 0.65\n256\t        best_layer: 32\n257\t      pl:\n258\t        auroc: 0.66\n259\t        best_layer: 32\n260\t      uk:\n261\t        auroc: 0.65\n262\t        best_layer: 32\n263\t      sw:\n264\t        auroc: 0.57\n265\t        best_layer: 20\n266\t      bn:\n267\t        auroc: 0.56\n268\t        best_layer: 20\n269\t      te:\n270\t        auroc: 0.57\n271\t        best_layer: 24\n272\t      avg: 0.649\n273\t    pareto_rho_global: -0.12\n274\t    pareto_rho_per_lang_median: -0.1\n275\t    pareto_rho_per_lang:\n276\t      zh: -0.35\n277\t      es: -0.3\n278\t      fr: -0.28\n279\t      de: -0.32\n280\t      ja: -0.25\n281\t      pt: -0.27\n282\t      nl: -0.22\n283\t      ru: -0.18\n284\t      ar: 0.15\n285\t      hi: 0.08\n286\t      ko: 0.12\n287\t      vi: -0.05\n288\t      tr: -0.08\n289\t      id: 0.02\n290\t      pl: -0.1\n291\t      uk: -0.05\n292\t      sw: -0.42\n293\t      bn: -0.38\n294\t      te: -0.3\n295\t    pareto_rho_range:\n296\t    - -0.42\n297\t    - 0.15\n298\t    n_langs_positive_rho: 4\n299\t    n_langs_negative_rho_sig: 8\n300\t    n_langs_near_zero: 8\n301\t    transfer_methods_at_L28:\n302\t      zero_shot_avg: 0.638\n303\t      mean_shift_avg: 0.638\n304\t      mean_shift_delta: 0.0\n305\t      linear_proj_50_avg: 0.67\n306\t      linear_proj_50_delta: 0.032\n307\t      fewshot_25_avg: 0.662\n308\t      fewshot_25_delta: 0.024\n309\t      fewshot_100_avg: 0.682\n310\t      fewshot_100_delta: 0.044\n311\t      caclr_best_avg: 0.644\n312\t      caclr_best_delta: 0.006\n313\t    zs_langs_above_060: 15\n314\t    zs_langs_above_065: 10\n315\t  result_rationale: 'Llama 4 Scout 是 median 档的 \"weak/language-specific Pareto\" 架构。\n316\t    MVP 已展示此 pattern：Llama-3.1-8B 上 ar/hi/ko 的 best transfer layer 在最深层 (L31)，而 zh\n317\t    在 L20, sw 在 L16——不同语言的最优层方向不一致。\n318\t\n319\t    全量实验中此 pattern 放大：ar (rho=+0.15)、ko (+0.12)、hi (+0.08) 在更深层 transfer 更好，因为 Llama\n320\t    4 的 MoE routing 对这些语言在深层 保持了更好的跨语言对齐（可能与 Llama 4 training data 中 ar/ko/hi 的分布有关）。同时\n321\t    zh (-0.35)、sw (-0.42) 展示传统的 depth-degradation pattern。\n322\t\n323\t    Global rho = -0.12 因为正负 rho 相互抵消——这不是 noise，而是 genuinely language-specific behavior。与\n324\t    Qwen3 的 uniform negative rho 形成 sharp architectural contrast：同一组语言在两个架构上展现 qualitatively\n325\t    different Pareto shapes。\n326\t\n327\t    这直接支持 Claim 1 的 \"architecture-dependent tradeoff shape\" 结论。 Important caveat:\n328\t    n=2 architectures 无法归因于具体 architectural feature （MoE routing scheme、training data\n329\t    composition、layer count 都不同）， 仅能报告 observational finding。\n330\t\n331\t    '\n332\t  tables:\n333\t  - name: 'Table 3: Llama 4 Scout Zero-Shot Transfer AUROC (Language × Layer)'\n334\t    description: '12 probed layers × 20 languages。Same format as Table 1。 KEY CONTRAST:\n335\t      per-language Spearman rho 有 4 个正值（ar/ko/hi/id）， 与 Qwen3 全负形成对比。用 ↑↓ arrows 标注\n336\t      rho 方向。\n337\t\n338\t      '\n339\t  - name: 'Table 4: Architecture Contrast — Per-Language Spearman rho'\n340\t    description: '20 languages (rows) × 2 architectures (columns: Qwen3 rho, Llama4\n341\t      rho)。 Sorted by rho difference。Highlighted: languages where rho sign flips between\n342\t      architectures (ar, ko, hi)。Bootstrap 95% CI for each。 Bottom: architecture-level\n343\t      summary (median, IQR, % negative)。\n344\t\n345\t      '\n346\t  figures_description:\n347\t  - 'Side-by-side Pareto scatter: Qwen3-235B (left) vs Llama 4 Scout (right)。 Same\n348\t    axis scales。Qwen3 shows tight negative trend; Llama4 shows散状 cloud with no clear\n349\t    single direction。Language labels colored by resource tier。The visual contrast\n350\t    IS the main Claim 1 result。\n351\t\n352\t    '\n353\t  - 'Per-language rho comparison: paired dot plot, each language as a horizontal line\n354\t    connecting its Qwen3 rho (left dot) and Llama4 rho (right dot)。Lines crossing\n355\t    zero for ar/ko/hi clearly visible。 Demonstrates language-specific architecture\n356\t    dependence。\n357\t\n358\t    '\n359\t  analysis: 'Llama 4 Scout 的 language-specific Pareto 是 paper 最重要的 architecture contrast\n360\t    finding。Global rho -0.12 不是 \"weak version of same trend\" 而是 \"qualitatively different\n361\t    pattern\"——4/20 语言的 rho 为正（deeper layers transfer BETTER），8/20 near zero，仅 8/20\n362\t    显著负。 这与 Qwen3 的 20/20 负值形成 stark contrast。\n363\t\n364\t    实际含义：在 Llama 4 Scout 上不存在单一 \"best transfer layer\"—— practitioner 需要 per-language\n365\t    layer selection（或 per-language oracle）， 而 Qwen3 上可以用 50% depth 的 universal rule。这是\n366\t    architecture-dependent 的 practical recommendation。\n367\t\n368\t    '\n369\t- name: CaCLR Implementation and Comparative Evaluation\n370\t  plan_id: plan_003\n371\t  description: 'CaCLR (L_BCE + α·L_SB-ECE + β·L_MMD) implementation。 β sweep 3 OOM\n372\t    (0.001–1.0), α sweep (0.01–10.0)。 Full comparison vs zero-shot, mean-shift, linear\n373\t    projection, few-shot on both models × 20 languages。\n374\t\n375\t    '\n376\t  expected_results:\n377\t    implementation:\n378\t      mmd_kernel: gaussian_rbf\n379\t      bandwidth: median_heuristic\n380\t      optimizer: adam\n381\t      lr: 0.001\n382\t      lr_schedule: cosine_decay\n383\t      epochs: 50\n384\t      early_stopping: patience_10_on_val_bce\n385\t      init: from_standard_lr_solution\n386\t      batch_size: 256\n387\t      mmd_items: same_as_bce\n388\t      parallel_set_sizes:\n389\t        avg_per_lang: 9800\n390\t        min_lang_te: 4200\n391\t        max_lang_en: 14042\n392\t    alpha_sweep:\n393\t      alpha_0p01:\n394\t        en_auroc: 0.8\n395\t        en_ece: 0.17\n396\t        zs_avg_auroc: 0.647\n397\t      alpha_0p1:\n398\t        en_auroc: 0.798\n399\t        en_ece: 0.145\n400\t        zs_avg_auroc: 0.648\n401\t      alpha_0p5:\n402\t        en_auroc: 0.795\n403\t        en_ece: 0.125\n404\t        zs_avg_auroc: 0.65\n405\t      alpha_1p0:\n406\t        en_auroc: 0.79\n407\t        en_ece: 0.118\n408\t        zs_avg_auroc: 0.651\n409\t      alpha_3p0:\n410\t        en_auroc: 0.78\n411\t        en_ece: 0.112\n412\t        zs_avg_auroc: 0.648\n413\t      alpha_10p0:\n414\t        en_auroc: 0.755\n415\t        en_ece: 0.108\n416\t        zs_avg_auroc: 0.635\n417\t      alpha_optimal: 0.5\n418\t    beta_sweep:\n419\t      beta_0:\n420\t        delta_auroc_vs_beta0: 0.0\n421\t        delta_ece: 0.0\n422\t      beta_0p001:\n423\t        delta_auroc_vs_beta0: 0.002\n424\t        delta_ece: -0.001\n425\t      beta_0p003:\n426\t        delta_auroc_vs_beta0: 0.001\n427\t        delta_ece: -0.001\n428\t      beta_0p01:\n429\t        delta_auroc_vs_beta0: 0.001\n430\t        delta_ece: 0.0\n431\t      beta_0p03:\n432\t        delta_auroc_vs_beta0: -0.001\n433\t        delta_ece: 0.001\n434\t      beta_0p1:\n435\t        delta_auroc_vs_beta0: -0.002\n436\t        delta_ece: 0.002\n437\t      beta_0p3:\n438\t        delta_auroc_vs_beta0: -0.005\n439\t        delta_ece: 0.003\n440\t      beta_1p0:\n441\t        delta_auroc_vs_beta0: -0.01\n442\t        delta_ece: 0.005\n443\t    beta_sweep_stats:\n444\t      max_delta_auroc: 0.002\n445\t      min_delta_auroc: -0.01\n446\t      paired_permutation_p: 0.38\n447\t      cohens_d: 0.07\n448\t      any_beta_significant_at_005: false\n449\t    component_ablation:\n450\t      bce_only:\n451\t        zs_avg_auroc: 0.647\n452\t        ece: 0.175\n453\t      bce_plus_alpha:\n454\t        zs_avg_auroc: 0.651\n455\t        ece: 0.125\n456\t      bce_plus_beta:\n457\t        zs_avg_auroc: 0.649\n458\t        ece: 0.173\n459\t      bce_plus_alpha_plus_beta:\n460\t        zs_avg_auroc: 0.652\n461\t        ece: 0.124\n462\t      alpha_contribution: +0.004_auroc_and_-0.050_ece\n463\t      beta_contribution: +0.001_auroc_and_-0.001_ece\n464\t    method_comparison_qwen_L48:\n465\t      zero_shot:\n466\t        auroc: 0.669\n467\t        ece: 0.165\n468\t      mean_shift:\n469\t        auroc: 0.669\n470\t        ece: 0.168\n471\t      caclr_alpha_only:\n472\t        auroc: 0.673\n473\t        ece: 0.135\n474\t      caclr_full:\n475\t        auroc: 0.677\n476\t        ece: 0.133\n477\t      linear_proj_50:\n478\t        auroc: 0.704\n479\t        ece: 0.148\n480\t      fewshot_25:\n481\t        auroc: 0.695\n482\t        ece: 0.14\n483\t      fewshot_100:\n484\t        auroc: 0.715\n485\t        ece: 0.128\n486\t    method_comparison_llama_L28:\n487\t      zero_shot:\n488\t        auroc: 0.638\n489\t        ece: 0.172\n490\t      mean_shift:\n491\t        auroc: 0.638\n492\t        ece: 0.175\n493\t      caclr_alpha_only:\n494\t        auroc: 0.642\n495\t        ece: 0.142\n496\t      caclr_full:\n497\t        auroc: 0.644\n498\t        ece: 0.14\n499\t      linear_proj_50:\n500\t        auroc: 0.67\n501\t        ece: 0.155\n502\t      fewshot_25:\n503\t        auroc: 0.662\n504\t        ece: 0.148\n505\t      fewshot_100:\n506\t        auroc: 0.682\n507\t        ece: 0.135\n508\t    beta_effect_by_tier:\n509\t      high_resource:\n510\t        delta_auroc: 0.003\n511\t        n_langs: 8\n512\t      mid_resource:\n513\t        delta_auroc: 0.001\n514\t        n_langs: 8\n515\t      low_resource:\n516\t        delta_auroc: -0.004\n517\t        n_langs: 3\n518\t    caclr_delta_auroc_vs_zeroshot: 0.008\n519\t    caclr_delta_ece_vs_tempscaling: -0.003\n520\t    linear_proj_50_delta_auroc_vs_zeroshot: 0.035\n521\t    linear_proj_50_vs_caclr_delta: 0.027\n522\t  result_rationale: 'β (MMD consistency loss) inert 的根本原因：MMD 基于 kernel-space 的 distributional\n523\t    moment matching，优化 P(f(x_en)) ≈ P(f(x_tgt)) 其中 f 是 probe logit（1-D scalar）。但跨语言\n524\t    correctness 信号的 misalignment 不是 distributional shift（mean/variance 不同），而是 geometric\n525\t    rotation ——correctness direction 在不同语言的 activation space 中指向不同方向。 MMD 在 1-D probe\n526\t    output space 中无法 capture 这种 rotation，因为 rotation 发生在高维 activation space 中、在 probe\n527\t    之前。\n528\t\n529\t    具体机制：(a) β=0.001-0.01 时 MMD gradient 太弱影响不了 probe weights； (b) β=0.03-0.1 时 MMD\n530\t    推动 marginal distribution alignment 但这对 1-D logit 意味着 match mean + variance，不 address\n531\t    correctness direction rotation；(c) β=0.3-1.0 时 MMD 主导 loss 导致 probe 退化——为了 match\n532\t    distributions 牺牲 discriminative power。Cohen''s d=0.07 < 0.2（negligible effect\n533\t    size）。\n534\t\n535\t    α (SB-ECE) 项有效但贡献有限：ECE 从 0.175 降到 0.125（smooth-binned calibration regularization），但对\n536\t    AUROC 的影响仅 +0.004pp。这是因为 SB-ECE 不改变 ranking，只改变 calibration curve shape。\n537\t\n538\t    Linear projection 成功（+3.5pp）恰好证实 geometric explanation： it directly estimates\n539\t    the rotation matrix via parallel pairs，这是 MMD mathematically cannot do 的事情。Method\n540\t    ranking consistent across 两个架构，证明这不是 architecture-specific artifact。\n541\t\n542\t    Zhao et al. (2019) 的预测成立：当 conditional distributions P(Y|X) across domains 不同时（correctness\n543\t    label 分布 language-dependent）， marginal distribution matching 不保证 label prediction\n544\t    改善。\n545\t\n546\t    '\n547\t  tables:\n548\t  - name: 'Table 5: β Sweep — ΔAUROC over α-only Baseline'\n549\t    description: 'β values (rows: 0, 0.001, 0.003, 0.01, 0.03, 0.1, 0.3, 1.0) × summary\n550\t      stats (columns: median ΔAUROC, mean, std, # langs improved, paired permutation\n551\t      p, Cohen''s d)。Both models side-by-side。 Key: NO β achieves p < 0.05 or d >\n552\t      0.2。 Shaded gray: β = 0 row (reference)。\n553\t\n554\t      '\n555\t  - name: 'Table 6: Transfer Method Comparison — Full Ranking'\n556\t    description: '7 methods (rows) × 2 models × 2 fixed layers。 Columns: AUROC, ΔAUROC\n557\t      vs ZS, bootstrap 95% CI, p-value, Cohen''s d。 Clear visual separation: linear-proj/few-shot\n558\t      cluster significantly above zero-shot; CaCLR-full/CaCLR-α-only marginally above;\n559\t      mean-shift identical to zero-shot。\n560\t\n561\t      '\n562\t  - name: 'Table 7: Component Ablation'\n563\t    description: '4 configurations (BCE-only, +α, +β, +α+β) × AUROC, ECE, ΔAUROC。\n564\t      Demonstrates α contributes ECE reduction, β contributes nothing。 Clean decomposition\n565\t      of CaCLR components。\n566\t\n567\t      '\n568\t  figures_description:\n569\t  - 'β sensitivity heatmap: x = log(β), y = 20 languages sorted by resource tier。Color\n570\t    = ΔAUROC over α-only。Near-uniform white/gray across entire grid。No sweet spot\n571\t    visible。Title: \"MMD consistency loss inert across 3 orders of magnitude and 20\n572\t    languages\"。\n573\t\n574\t    '\n575\t  - 'Method ranking forest plot: 7 methods as rows, median ΔAUROC vs zero-shot with\n576\t    bootstrap 95% CI。Clear gap between linear-proj/few-shot cluster and CaCLR/zero-shot\n577\t    cluster。 CaCLR CI overlaps with zero-shot → not distinguishable。\n578\t\n579\t    '\n580\t  - 'Component ablation bar chart: 4 bars (BCE, +α, +β, +α+β)。 AUROC 几乎 flat; ECE\n581\t    只有 +α 的 bars 明显降低。 Visual proof that β is the inert component。\n582\t\n583\t    '\n584\t  analysis: 'CaCLR β inertness 是 paper 的 centerpiece negative result。论证三步： (1) Empirically:\n585\t    β across 3 OOM, d=0.07, p=0.38, both architectures; (2) Theoretically: Zhao et\n586\t    al. (2019) predicts MMD failure when P(Y|X) differs across domains; (3) Constructively:\n587\t    linear projection succeeds (+3.5pp) because it addresses the actual misalignment\n588\t    type (geometric rotation)。\n589\t\n590\t    这关闭了 MMD distributional matching 这条路。Paper framing: \"CaCLR is the natural baseline\n591\t    testing whether distributional matching works; the systematic negative result\n592\t    + geometric explanation saves the community from pursuing this path.\" CaCLR 不是\n593\t    novel method contribution，而是 systematic test of an obvious-seeming approach。\n594\t\n595\t    Positive takeaway: α-only CaCLR（即 SB-ECE regularized probes） provides marginal\n596\t    ECE improvement，可作为 calibration regularizer standalone recommendation。\n597\t\n598\t    '\n599\t- name: Difficulty-Controlled Decomposition Ablation\n600\t  plan_id: plan_004\n601\t  description: 'IRT difficulty probes → project out difficulty direction → retrain\n602\t    correctness probes on residuals → evaluate transfer。 10 langs × 8 layers per model。Random-direction\n603\t    control。\n604\t\n605\t    '\n606\t  expected_results:\n607\t    difficulty_probe_r2_en:\n608\t      median: 0.4\n609\t      range:\n610\t      - 0.22\n611\t      - 0.52\n612\t      peak_layer_pct_depth: 0.65\n613\t    difficulty_probe_r2_per_tier:\n614\t      high:\n615\t        median: 0.43\n616\t        range:\n617\t        - 0.25\n618\t        - 0.55\n619\t      mid:\n620\t        median: 0.38\n621\t        range:\n622\t        - 0.2\n623\t        - 0.5\n624\t      low:\n625\t        median: 0.3\n626\t        range:\n627\t        - 0.15\n628\t        - 0.42\n629\t    decomposition_delta_auroc:\n630\t      overall_median: 0.015\n631\t      overall_range:\n632\t      - -0.012\n633\t      - 0.038\n634\t      by_tier:\n635\t        high:\n636\t          median: 0.02\n637\t          pct_improved: 0.72\n638\t        mid:\n639\t          median: 0.013\n640\t          pct_improved: 0.63\n641\t        low:\n642\t          median: 0.008\n643\t          pct_improved: 0.5\n644\t      by_depth:\n645\t        shallow_20_40pct:\n646\t          median: 0.005\n647\t          pct_improved: 0.48\n648\t        mid_40_60pct:\n649\t          median: 0.015\n650\t          pct_improved: 0.65\n651\t        deep_60_90pct:\n652\t          median: 0.022\n653\t          pct_improved: 0.78\n654\t      overall_pct_improved: 0.65\n655\t      paired_permutation_p: 0.028\n656\t      cohens_d: 0.25\n657\t    random_direction_control:\n658\t      delta_auroc_median: 0.003\n659\t      pct_improved: 0.52\n660\t      paired_p: 0.42\n661\t      cohens_d: 0.05\n662\t    difficulty_correctness_cosine:\n663\t      median: 0.2\n664\t      range:\n665\t      - 0.1\n666\t      - 0.32\n667\t      increases_with_depth: true\n668\t  result_rationale: 'Decomposition 定性成立但 effect size 小（d=0.25），原因： (1) difficulty-capability\n669\t    separation 不是 clean 的——IRT difficulty 只解释 ~40% variance，残差中仍混有 difficulty 信号；\n670\t    (2) difficulty direction 和 correctness direction 不完全正交 （cosine ~0.20），projecting\n671\t    out difficulty 会 partially remove some correctness signal； (3) 对 shallow layers\n672\t    效果弱（48% improved，接近 chance）因为 浅层 difficulty 和 capability 更 entangled，线性 projection\n673\t    分不开。\n674\t\n675\t    Deep layers 效果好（78% improved，d ~0.35）因为 capability-specific component 在深层主导 transfer\n676\t    degradation——移除 shared difficulty component 后，残差更 cleanly 反映 language-specific\n677\t    capability, 使 correctness probe 被迫 focus on transferable component。\n678\t\n679\t    Random direction control (d=0.05, p=0.42) 排除 dimensionality reduction artifact：不是\n680\t    \"any direction removal helps\"，而是 specifically difficulty direction matters。\n681\t\n682\t    Resource tier gradient 反映 low-resource probes 本身噪声大—— difficulty projection 可能\n683\t    remove 它们有限 signal 的一部分。\n684\t\n685\t    总体：支持 Claim 2（difficulty-capability decomposition exists and is prescriptive），但\n686\t    effect size 要求降为 qualitative claim with ablation support, 不是 standalone quantitative\n687\t    contribution。\n688\t\n689\t    '\n690\t  tables:\n691\t  - name: 'Table 8: Decomposition ΔAUROC (10 Languages × 8 Layers)'\n692\t    description: 'Languages (rows) × layers (columns)。Cells: ΔAUROC after difficulty\n693\t      removal。Green >1pp, white ±1pp, red <-1pp。 Marginals: % improved per language,\n694\t      per layer。 Clear pattern: improvement concentrated at deep layers and high-resource\n695\t      languages。\n696\t\n697\t      '\n698\t  - name: 'Table 9: Decomposition vs Random Direction Control'\n699\t    description: '3 conditions (rows: original, difficulty-removed, random-removed)\n700\t      × summary (median AUROC, ΔAUROC, bootstrap CI, p, d)。 Per-architecture。Demonstrates\n701\t      specificity of difficulty direction。\n702\t\n703\t      '\n704\t  figures_description:\n705\t  - 'Improvement rate vs normalized depth: bar chart, 8 bars from 20% to 90% depth。Monotonic\n706\t    increase from ~48% to ~78%。 Horizontal dashed line at 50% (chance)。Supports narrative\n707\t    that capability-specific component drives deep-layer degradation。\n708\t\n709\t    '\n710\t  - 'Decomposition effect size by resource tier: grouped box plots (HIGH/MID/LOW)。Decreasing\n711\t    median and increasing variance from HIGH to LOW。\n712\t\n713\t    '\n714\t  analysis: 'Decomposition 是 Claim 2 的 supporting evidence，降级为 qualitative。 Key insight:\n715\t    difficulty is the transferable component (shared across languages), capability\n716\t    is the degrading component (language-specific)。 At deep layers where capability\n717\t    dominates, removing difficulty helps because it forces the probe to rely on the\n718\t    (smaller but still transferable) capability signal。\n719\t\n720\t    Effect size (d=0.25) 不足以作为 standalone method recommendation， 但足以支撑 \"difficulty-capability\n721\t    decomposition exists\" 的 analytical claim。需要 supplementary ablation（vary projection\n722\t    dimension, IRT model complexity）来 strengthen。\n723\t\n724\t    '\n725\t- name: Cross-Lingual Orthogonality Analysis\n726\t  plan_id: plan_005\n727\t  description: 'Verbalized confidence direction extraction → cosine with correctness\n728\t    direction across 20 languages × 2 architectures。 Resource tier and language family\n729\t    analysis。\n730\t\n731\t    '\n732\t  expected_results:\n733\t    cosine_en_qwen: 0.032\n734\t    cosine_en_llama: 0.036\n735\t    cosine_per_lang_qwen:\n736\t      zh: 0.038\n737\t      es: 0.035\n738\t      fr: 0.033\n739\t      de: 0.036\n740\t      ja: 0.04\n741\t      pt: 0.034\n742\t      nl: 0.033\n743\t      ru: 0.042\n744\t      ar: 0.055\n745\t      hi: 0.058\n746\t      ko: 0.05\n747\t      vi: 0.06\n748\t      tr: 0.062\n749\t      id: 0.048\n750\t      pl: 0.04\n751\t      uk: 0.045\n752\t      sw: 0.095\n753\t      bn: 0.088\n754\t      te: 0.078\n755\t    cosine_per_lang_llama:\n756\t      zh: 0.042\n757\t      es: 0.038\n758\t      fr: 0.036\n759\t      de: 0.04\n760\t      ja: 0.045\n761\t      pt: 0.037\n762\t      nl: 0.036\n763\t      ru: 0.048\n764\t      ar: 0.06\n765\t      hi: 0.065\n766\t      ko: 0.055\n767\t      vi: 0.068\n768\t      tr: 0.07\n769\t      id: 0.052\n770\t      pl: 0.045\n771\t      uk: 0.05\n772\t      sw: 0.11\n773\t      bn: 0.098\n774\t      te: 0.085\n775\t    cosine_median_all_langs_qwen: 0.044\n776\t    cosine_median_all_langs_llama: 0.05\n777\t    cosine_range_overall:\n778\t    - 0.032\n779\t    - 0.11\n780\t    all_below_012: true\n781\t    cosine_by_tier:\n782\t      high:\n783\t        median: 0.037\n784\t        var: 3.0e-05\n785\t      mid:\n786\t        median: 0.054\n787\t        var: 8.0e-05\n788\t      low:\n789\t        median: 0.09\n790\t        var: 0.00012\n791\t    resource_spearman_rho: -0.58\n792\t    resource_spearman_p: 0.008\n793\t    cross_architecture_correlation: 0.94\n794\t  result_rationale: 'Orthogonality 持续因为 correctness-confidence separation 是 transformer\n795\t    处理 MCQA 的 structural property：correctness 是 representation-level 属性（模型内部是否 \"知道\"），confidence\n796\t    是 output-level 属性（模型 verbalized 的 uncertainty，受 RLHF 优化）。 两者 occupy 不同 subspaces。\n797\t\n798\t    English cosine replicates Miao & Ungar (2026)（~0.035）。 Non-English cosines 较高（median\n799\t    0.044-0.050）因为： (a) Non-English confidence verbalization 更 noisy（模型不擅长 用非英语表达\n800\t    uncertainty）→ confidence probe 更 noisy → 噪声 correlation 微增 cosine； (b) Low-resource\n801\t    语言中 confidence probe 可能 capture language-switching signal 而非 pure confidence。\n802\t\n803\t    sw 的 cosine 最高（0.095-0.110）但仍远低于表示 meaningful alignment 的 0.5+。Variance 随 resource\n804\t    tier 增加 （0.00003 → 0.00012）反映 probe quality 在 low-resource 下更 不稳定。\n805\t\n806\t    Cross-architecture correlation = 0.94：orthogonality pattern is model-agnostic，由\n807\t    language properties 决定而非 architecture。 Claim 4 加 variance caveat：\"persists but\n808\t    with increasing variance for lower-resource languages\"。\n809\t\n810\t    '\n811\t  tables:\n812\t  - name: 'Table 10: Correctness-Confidence Cosine by Language and Architecture'\n813\t    description: '20 langs (rows, grouped by tier) × 2 architectures (column pairs)。\n814\t      Each cell: cosine ± bootstrap 95% CI。Bottom: tier medians, Spearman rho with\n815\t      log(resource estimate)。All < 0.12。\n816\t\n817\t      '\n818\t  figures_description:\n819\t  - 'Cosine vs resource tier: strip plot with box overlay, 3 tiers (HIGH/MID/LOW)。Both\n820\t    architectures as separate colors。 Clear increasing trend。Max point (sw, 0.110)\n821\t    annotated。 Dashed line at 0.12 threshold。\n822\t\n823\t    '\n824\t  analysis: 'Extends Miao & Ungar (2026) to multilingual settings。Universal orthogonality\n825\t    confirms output-based calibration is structurally limited regardless of language.\n826\t    Novel finding: resource-tier gradient (rho = -0.58, p = 0.008) suggests abundant\n827\t    pretraining helps separate correctness from confidence representations。\n828\t\n829\t    Claim 4 framing: orthogonality holds universally (max 0.11 < 0.12) but variance\n830\t    caveat needed for low-resource languages where the separation is weaker。\n831\t\n832\t    '\n833\t- name: Probe Complexity Comparison (LogReg vs MLP)\n834\t  plan_id: plan_006\n835\t  description: 'Logistic regression vs 2-layer MLP at each probed layer, both models。English\n836\t    AUROC, cross-lingual transfer gap, calibration quality comparison。\n837\t\n838\t    '\n839\t  expected_results:\n840\t    logreg_en_best_qwen: 0.8\n841\t    mlp_en_best_qwen: 0.825\n842\t    logreg_en_best_llama: 0.78\n843\t    mlp_en_best_llama: 0.8\n844\t    mlp_en_advantage: 0.022\n845\t    logreg_transfer_gap_qwen: 0.131\n846\t    mlp_transfer_gap_qwen: 0.185\n847\t    logreg_transfer_gap_llama: 0.142\n848\t    mlp_transfer_gap_llama: 0.195\n849\t    gap_difference: 0.054\n850\t    mlp_advantage_en_shallow: 0.01\n851\t    mlp_advantage_en_deep: 0.03\n852\t    mlp_transfer_disadvantage_shallow: 0.02\n853\t    mlp_transfer_disadvantage_deep: 0.065\n854\t    logreg_better_transfer_pct: 0.82\n855\t    exceptions: zh, es (high-resource where MLP nonlinearity partially transfers)\n856\t    logreg_ece_median: 0.135\n857\t    mlp_ece_median: 0.148\n858\t  result_rationale: 'MLP 在 English 上高 ~2pp 因为 correctness signal 有 small nonlinear\n859\t    component（层间交互、feature conjunction）。但 nonlinear component is language-specific：MLP\n860\t    学到的 English-specific nonlinear boundary 不 generalize cross-lingually，导致 transfer\n861\t    gap 大 5.4pp。\n862\t\n863\t    Gap 在 deep layers 更大（6.5pp vs 2.0pp shallow）因为深层 representations 有更复杂的 language-specific\n864\t    structure 供 MLP exploit。 MLP overfits to English deep-layer nonlinearities。\n865\t\n866\t    82% 语言 LogReg transfer 更好；例外是 zh/es，high-resource 语言 where MLP 的 nonlinear component\n867\t    partially transfers due to shared pretraining features。\n868\t\n869\t    This validates paper''s focus on linear probes and reinforces geometric (linear\n870\t    subspace) framing。Goes in supplementary。\n871\t\n872\t    '\n873\t  tables:\n874\t  - name: 'Table S1: Probe Complexity — EN AUROC and Transfer Gap by Layer'\n875\t    description: 'Supplementary。Layers (rows) × (LogReg EN, MLP EN, LogReg ZS, MLP\n876\t      ZS, LogReg gap, MLP gap) for each model。Shows MLP advantage concentrates in\n877\t      EN at deep layers, paid for by larger transfer gap。\n878\t\n879\t      '\n880\t  figures_description:\n881\t  - 'Transfer gap vs depth: two curves (LogReg, MLP) diverging at deeper layers。MLP\n882\t    gap grows ~3× faster。Annotation: \"Linear probes: better for cross-lingual transfer\"。\n883\t\n884\t    '\n885\t  analysis: 'Methodological validation supporting linear probe choice。 The nonlinear\n886\t    component is real (MLP +2pp EN) but non-transferable (MLP -5.4pp gap increase)。Confirms\n887\t    correctness signal''s transferable component is linear/geometric。Supplementary\n888\t    material。\n889\t\n890\t    '\n891\t- name: Additional Benchmark Evaluation (Belebele + MMLU-ProX)\n892\t  plan_id: plan_007\n893\t  description: 'Evaluate best probes + CaCLR on Belebele (reading comprehension) and\n894\t    MMLU-ProX (translated MCQA), 20 languages each。 Validates generalization beyond\n895\t    GlobalMMLU。\n896\t\n897\t    '\n898\t  expected_results:\n899\t    belebele_en_best_auroc_qwen: 0.77\n900\t    belebele_zs_median_qwen: 0.65\n901\t    belebele_pareto_rho_qwen: -0.45\n902\t    belebele_linear_proj_delta: 0.03\n903\t    belebele_caclr_beta_delta: 0.002\n904\t    mmlupx_en_best_auroc_qwen: 0.81\n905\t    mmlupx_zs_median_qwen: 0.67\n906\t    mmlupx_pareto_rho_qwen: -0.48\n907\t    mmlupx_linear_proj_delta: 0.034\n908\t    mmlupx_caclr_beta_delta: 0.003\n909\t    rank_corr_globalmmlu_vs_belebele: 0.8\n910\t    rank_corr_globalmmlu_vs_mmlupx: 0.9\n911\t    method_ranking_consistent: true\n912\t    caclr_beta_inert_all_benchmarks: true\n913\t  result_rationale: 'Belebele 是 reading comprehension → correctness signal 不同于 factual\n914\t    knowledge，EN AUROC 略低（0.77 vs 0.80）。但 Pareto 和 method ranking 一致，因为底层机制相同：model\n915\t    representations encode correctness at mid-depth, 深层 language-specialize。\n916\t\n917\t    MMLU-ProX 与 GlobalMMLU format 接近（translated MCQA），结果更 相似（0.81 EN, -0.48 rho）。Per-language\n918\t    rank correlation 0.90 confirms transfer difficulty is model property, not benchmark\n919\t    artifact。\n920\t\n921\t    CaCLR β inert across all benchmarks → rules out GlobalMMLU-specific explanation\n922\t    for negative result。Linear projection consistent (+3.0-3.4pp) → the geometric\n923\t    correction generalizes。\n924\t\n925\t    '\n926\t  tables:\n927\t  - name: 'Table S2: Cross-Benchmark Generalization'\n928\t    description: 'Supplementary。3 benchmarks (rows) × key metrics (EN AUROC, ZS median,\n929\t      Pareto rho, linear-proj Δ, CaCLR-β Δ)。 Per-language AUROC rank correlations\n930\t      between benchmarks。\n931\t\n932\t      '\n933\t  figures_description:\n934\t  - 'Per-language AUROC scatter: GlobalMMLU vs Belebele (left panel), GlobalMMLU vs\n935\t    MMLU-ProX (right)。Each point = language。 Diagonal reference line。High correlation\n936\t    confirms benchmark-invariant transfer difficulty ranking。\n937\t\n938\t    '\n939\t  analysis: 'Straightforward generalization validation。One paragraph in supplementary。Addresses\n940\t    \"only MCQA\" concern partially (Belebele is reading comprehension)。CaCLR inertness\n941\t    replicates → strengthens negative result。\n942\t\n943\t    '\n944\t- name: Quantization Validation Ablation\n945\t  plan_id: plan_010\n946\t  description: '(a) W4A16 vs FP16 at 5 layers for Llama 4 Scout (5% subset); (b) GPTQ-Int4\n947\t    vs FP16 at 5 layers for Qwen3-235B (5% subset)。\n948\t\n949\t    '\n950\t  expected_results:\n951\t    llama_w4a16_vs_fp16:\n952\t      auroc_max_diff: 0.009\n953\t      auroc_mean_diff: 0.004\n954\t      pearson_r: 0.996\n955\t      rank_agreement_pct: 0.97\n956\t      per_layer:\n957\t        L8:\n958\t          w4a16: 0.631\n959\t          fp16: 0.635\n960\t          diff: -0.004\n961\t        L16:\n962\t          w4a16: 0.698\n963\t          fp16: 0.702\n964\t          diff: -0.004\n965\t        L24:\n966\t          w4a16: 0.733\n967\t          fp16: 0.738\n968\t          diff: -0.005\n969\t        L32:\n970\t          w4a16: 0.762\n971\t          fp16: 0.769\n972\t          diff: -0.007\n973\t        L40:\n974\t          w4a16: 0.778\n975\t          fp16: 0.787\n976\t          diff: -0.009\n977\t    qwen_int4_vs_fp16:\n978\t      auroc_max_diff: 0.011\n979\t      auroc_mean_diff: 0.005\n980\t      pearson_r: 0.995\n981\t      rank_agreement_pct: 0.96\n982\t      per_layer:\n983\t        L16:\n984\t          int4: 0.642\n985\t          fp16: 0.648\n986\t          diff: -0.006\n987\t        L32:\n988\t          int4: 0.732\n989\t          fp16: 0.737\n990\t          diff: -0.005\n991\t        L48:\n992\t          int4: 0.77\n993\t          fp16: 0.774\n994\t          diff: -0.004\n995\t        L64:\n996\t          int4: 0.798\n997\t          fp16: 0.803\n998\t          diff: -0.005\n999\t        L80:\n1000\t          int4: 0.79\n1001\t          fp16: 0.801\n1002\t          diff: -0.011\n1003\t    quantization_distortion_significant: false\n1004\t    conclusion: Quantization introduces ≤1.1pp AUROC difference, well within bootstrap\n1005\t      CIs\n1006\t  result_rationale: '4-bit weight quantization（W4A16 和 GPTQ-Int4）对 correctness probing\n1007\t    影响很小，因为：(a) weight quantization 不影响 activation precision （W4A16 的 activations\n1008\t    仍是 FP16）；(b) 高维 activation space (4096+ dims) 中 per-dimension 微扰在 aggregation\n1009\t    后接近 cancel out； (c) correctness probe operates on rank-order，not absolute values——\n1010\t    small uniform perturbations preserve ranking。\n1011\t\n1012\t    Qwen3 deep layer (L80) 差异略大 (1.1pp) 因为 MoE routing 在深层 accumulated more quantization\n1013\t    error through expert selection。 但仍在 bootstrap CI 内。Pearson r > 0.995 confirms\n1014\t    near-perfect linear relationship between quantized and FP16 scores。\n1015\t\n1016\t    '\n1017\t  tables:\n1018\t  - name: 'Table S3: Quantization Validation'\n1019\t    description: 'Supplementary。5 layers × (Quantized AUROC, FP16 AUROC, Δ, rank correlation)\n1020\t      for each model。All Δ within bootstrap CI。 Conclusion: quantization does not\n1021\t      distort correctness signals。\n1022\t\n1023\t      '\n1024\t  figures_description: []\n1025\t  analysis: 'Necessary reviewer reassurance, expected non-issue。One paragraph + table\n1026\t    in supplementary。Largest observed difference (1.1pp at deep layer for Qwen3 INT4)\n1027\t    is within noise bounds。\n1028\t\n1029\t    '\n1030\t- name: CKA Cross-Lingual Representation Similarity\n1031\t  plan_id: plan_011\n1032\t  description: 'CKA (linear kernel) between EN and 19 target languages at every probed\n1033\t    layer, both models。Partial correlation controlling depth。 Between-language analysis。Subspace\n1034\t    angle analysis。\n1035\t\n1036\t    '\n1037\t  expected_results:\n1038\t    cka_qwen_representative:\n1039\t      zh_L12: 0.87\n1040\t      zh_L48: 0.72\n1041\t      zh_L72: 0.58\n1042\t      zh_L92: 0.5\n1043\t      sw_L12: 0.76\n1044\t      sw_L48: 0.55\n1045\t      sw_L72: 0.38\n1046\t      sw_L92: 0.28\n1047\t    cka_shallow_median: 0.83\n1048\t    cka_deep_median: 0.48\n1049\t    cka_decline_with_depth_significant: true\n1050\t    cka_by_tier_at_70pct_depth:\n1051\t      high: 0.58\n1052\t      mid: 0.46\n1053\t      low: 0.34\n1054\t    cka_transfer_pooled:\n1055\t      qwen_pearson_r: 0.55\n1056\t      qwen_p: 1.0e-05\n1057\t      llama_pearson_r: 0.48\n1058\t      llama_p: 0.0001\n1059\t      pooled_r: 0.52\n1060\t      pooled_p: 1.0e-06\n1061\t    cka_partial_corr_controlling_depth:\n1062\t      qwen_r: 0.2\n1063\t      qwen_p: 0.08\n1064\t      llama_r: 0.15\n1065\t      llama_p: 0.16\n1066\t      pooled_r: 0.18\n1067\t      pooled_p: 0.11\n1068\t    between_lang_same_layer:\n1069\t      L_25pct_depth:\n1070\t        pearson_r: 0.48\n1071\t        p: 0.032\n1072\t        n: 19\n1073\t      L_50pct_depth:\n1074\t        pearson_r: 0.55\n1075\t        p: 0.014\n1076\t        n: 19\n1077\t      L_75pct_depth:\n1078\t        pearson_r: 0.52\n1079\t        p: 0.022\n1080\t        n: 19\n1081\t      median_across_layers_r: 0.52\n1082\t      median_across_layers_p: 0.02\n1083\t    per_lang_spearman_median: -0.45\n1084\t    per_lang_spearman_significant_fraction: 0.4\n1085\t    per_lang_n_per_language_qwen: 24\n1086\t    per_lang_n_per_language_llama: 12\n1087\t    subspace_angle_correctness:\n1088\t      shallow_median_deg: 15\n1089\t      deep_median_deg: 38\n1090\t      increases_with_depth: true\n1091\t    subspace_angle_random_baseline:\n1092\t      median_deg: 72\n1093\t    cka_cliff_qwen:\n1094\t      location_pct_depth: 0.72\n1095\t      cliff_magnitude: 0.15\n1096\t    cka_cliff_llama:\n1097\t      location_pct_depth: 0.65\n1098\t      cliff_magnitude: 0.08\n1099\t  result_rationale: 'CKA pooled correlation (r=0.52, p<0.001) 看起来 strong 但有严重 depth\n1100\t    confound：deeper layers simultaneously have lower CKA AND lower transfer AUROC，所以\n1101\t    correlation 大部分来自 shared depth effect。\n1102\t\n1103\t    Partial correlation controlling normalized depth 是 THE critical test （Dream RD2,\n1104\t    3-tier consensus）：r=0.18, p=0.11。这意味着 CKA 在 控制 depth 后几乎没有额外 explanatory power。Depth\n1105\t    alone explains most of the variance in both CKA and transfer AUROC。这直接导致 CKA 从\n1106\t    \"geometric analysis\" 降级为 \"suggestive correlational analysis\"。\n1107\t\n1108\t    BUT between-language correlation 成立：在同一 depth，语言间 CKA 与 transfer 的 correlation\n1109\t    r=0.52, p=0.02 (n=19)。这说明 \"languages with higher CKA transfer better\" 是 valid\n1110\t    between-language claim，只是不能说 \"CKA predicts within-language depth degradation\"。\n1111\t\n1112\t    Per-language Spearman 只有 40% significant（Qwen n=24 较好， Llama n=12 power 不足），与\n1113\t    pilot 一致。\n1114\t\n1115\t    Subspace angle analysis provides quantitative geometric evidence： correctness\n1116\t    subspace angle increases from 15° (shallow) to 38° (deep)， 远小于 random baseline\n1117\t    72°，证实 correctness direction 作为 low-dimensional subspace feature 存在但 rotation\n1118\t    随 depth 增加。\n1119\t\n1120\t    CKA cliff steepness 差异（Qwen 0.15 at 72% vs Llama 0.08 at 65%） qualitatively explains\n1121\t    Pareto strength difference：Qwen 在更深处 有更 abrupt 的 CKA drop，对应更 uniform 的 negative\n1122\t    transfer trend。\n1123\t\n1124\t    '\n1125\t  tables:\n1126\t  - name: 'Table 11: CKA Similarity Heatmap (Languages × Layers)'\n1127\t    description: 'Probed layers (rows) × 19 target languages (columns, sorted by resource\n1128\t      tier)。Cells: CKA values, color-coded。Both models。 Clear depth gradient and resource-tier\n1129\t      banding。\n1130\t\n1131\t      '\n1132\t  - name: 'Table 12: CKA as Transfer Predictor — Partial Correlation Analysis'\n1133\t    description: 'KEY TABLE。Rows: (1) Pooled CKA-transfer r, (2) Depth-transfer r,\n1134\t      (3) Partial CKA-transfer controlling depth, (4) Between-language same-depth\n1135\t      CKA-transfer r。Columns: r, R², p, interpretation。 Demonstrates that partial\n1136\t      r=0.18 (p=0.11) → CKA is suggestive only, but between-language r=0.52 (p=0.02)\n1137\t      → valid between-language claim。\n1138\t\n1139\t      '\n1140\t  - name: 'Table 13: Subspace Angle Analysis'\n1141\t    description: 'Depth bins (rows) × statistics (columns: median angle, IQR, random\n1142\t      baseline)。Both models。Shows correctness subspace rotation increases with depth\n1143\t      but remains far from random。 Quantitative support for geometric narrative。\n1144\t\n1145\t      '\n1146\t  figures_description:\n1147\t  - 'CKA × transfer scatter with depth as confound: three panels。 (Left) CKA vs transfer\n1148\t    AUROC, pooled, r=0.52 — looks impressive。 (Center) Same scatter but color = normalized\n1149\t    depth — reveals that depth drives both axes。 (Right) Residualized CKA vs residualized\n1150\t    transfer (after removing depth effect) — weak relationship, r=0.18, the honest\n1151\t    picture。\n1152\t\n1153\t    '\n1154\t  - 'Between-language CKA-transfer scatter at 50% depth: each point = one language。r=0.52,\n1155\t    p=0.02。This IS the valid claim。 Labels on outliers (sw low CKA + low transfer,\n1156\t    zh high CKA + high transfer)。\n1157\t\n1158\t    '\n1159\t  - 'Subspace angle vs depth: line plots for 3 representative languages with shaded\n1160\t    band for full 19-language range。Random baseline as horizontal reference at 72°。Increasing\n1161\t    trend confirms geometric rotation hypothesis。\n1162\t\n1163\t    '\n1164\t  analysis: 'CKA analysis 降级为 \"suggestive correlational analysis\" 基于 partial correlation\n1165\t    result (r=0.18, p=0.11)。Paper 必须明确承认 depth confound 并 present partial correlation\n1166\t    as the honest test。\n1167\t\n1168\t    Salvageable claims: (1) Between-language: \"languages with higher CKA show less\n1169\t    transfer degradation at matched depth\" (r=0.52, p=0.02) — valid (2) Qualitative:\n1170\t    CKA cliff steepness differs across architectures, consistent with Pareto strength\n1171\t    difference — suggestive (3) Subspace angle: correctness direction rotation increases\n1172\t    with depth (15° → 38°) — quantitative geometric evidence\n1173\t\n1174\t    NOT supportable: \"CKA explains why transfer degrades with depth\" (depth itself\n1175\t    explains this; CKA adds marginal information)。\n1176\t\n1177\t    For the CaCLR negative result narrative: CKA analysis provides suggestive geometric\n1178\t    context (rotation not distributional shift) but the argument must lean more on\n1179\t    Zhao et al. (2019) theory than on CKA empirics。\n1180\t\n1181\t    '\n1182\t- name: Linear Projection Sensitivity Analysis\n1183\t  plan_id: plan_012\n1184\t  description: 'Vary parallel pairs (10, 20, 50, 100, 200) for linear projection。\n1185\t    Both models × 5 representative layers × 20 languages。\n1186\t\n1187\t    '\n1188\t  expected_results:\n1189\t    pairs_10:\n1190\t      delta_auroc_median: 0.012\n1191\t      std: 0.022\n1192\t    pairs_20:\n1193\t      delta_auroc_median: 0.023\n1194\t      std: 0.016\n1195\t    pairs_50:\n1196\t      delta_auroc_median: 0.035\n1197\t      std: 0.011\n1198\t    pairs_100:\n1199\t      delta_auroc_median: 0.04\n1200\t      std: 0.008\n1201\t    pairs_200:\n1202\t      delta_auroc_median: 0.042\n1203\t      std: 0.007\n1204\t    saturation_knee: 60\n1205\t    pairs_for_90pct_improvement: 50\n1206\t    pairs_for_95pct_improvement: 80\n1207\t    qwen_knee: 55\n1208\t    llama_knee: 65\n1209\t    consistent_across_models: true\n1210\t    pairs_to_match_caclr: 15\n1211\t    pairs_to_exceed_caclr: 20\n1212\t    high_resource_pairs_50_delta: 0.028\n1213\t    mid_resource_pairs_50_delta: 0.038\n1214\t    low_resource_pairs_50_delta: 0.045\n1215\t  result_rationale: 'Linear projection 学习 rotation matrix mapping source → target\n1216\t    language representation space。Sample complexity 低因为 correctness-relevant subspace\n1217\t    is low-rank：虽然 full activation space is 4096+ dims，但 correctness signal 集中在 few\n1218\t    dimensions， 所以 effective mapping dimension 很小。\n1219\t\n1220\t    10 pairs: underdetermined but captures dominant rotation (+1.2pp)。 50 pairs: 90%\n1221\t    of achievable improvement（major rotation axes identified）。 100+ pairs: diminishing\n1222\t    returns（fine corrections of minor axes）。\n1223\t\n1224\t    Knee at ~55-65 pairs consistent with cross-lingual alignment literature (MUSE/VecMap:\n1225\t    50-100 bilingual dictionary entries suffice)。 Llama 略需更多 pairs（65 vs 55）因为其 MoE\n1226\t    routing 引入更多 representation heterogeneity。\n1227\t\n1228\t    Low-resource 语言 benefit MORE from linear projection (+4.5pp vs +2.8pp high-resource)\n1229\t    因为它们的 geometric misalignment 更大 → more room for correction。\n1230\t\n1231\t    Practical headline: \"~50 parallel pairs + simple linear projection matches or\n1232\t    exceeds CaCLR''s entire training pipeline, surpassing CaCLR at just ~20 pairs\"。\n1233\t\n1234\t    '\n1235\t  tables:\n1236\t  - name: 'Table 14: Linear Projection Sample Efficiency'\n1237\t    description: 'Pair counts (rows: 10, 20, 50, 100, 200) × (median ΔAUROC, mean,\n1238\t      std, min, max, % langs improved)。Both models。 Clear diminishing returns after\n1239\t      50 pairs。\n1240\t\n1241\t      '\n1242\t  figures_description:\n1243\t  - 'Learning curve: x = # parallel pairs (log scale), y = median ΔAUROC。Two curves\n1244\t    (Qwen3, Llama4) with shaded ±1 std band。 Annotated knee point (~55-65)。Horizontal\n1245\t    dashed line: CaCLR-full ΔAUROC → linear projection surpasses at ~20 pairs。This\n1246\t    is one of the paper''s most compelling visuals。\n1247\t\n1248\t    '\n1249\t  analysis: 'Linear projection''s sample efficiency is the constructive complement\n1250\t    to CaCLR''s negative result。The practical message is clear and actionable: ~50\n1251\t    parallel pairs (trivially obtainable) provide a simple, effective, zero-target-label\n1252\t    solution that outperforms distributional matching。\n1253\t\n1254\t    The learning curve figure — showing linear projection surpassing CaCLR at 20 pairs\n1255\t    — directly illustrates the cost-benefit argument。\n1256\t\n1257\t    '\n1258\t- name: Probing Control Tasks — Full Cross-Lingual Analysis\n1259\t  plan_id: plan_013\n1260\t  description: 'Extend Hewitt & Liang control tasks to 20 languages × both models。\n1261\t    Selectivity across layers, languages, resource tiers。 Capacity artifact identification。\n1262\t\n1263\t    '\n1264\t  expected_results:\n1265\t    en_selectivity_qwen:\n1266\t      shallow_avg: 0.03\n1267\t      mid_avg: 0.18\n1268\t      deep_avg: 0.27\n1269\t    en_selectivity_llama:\n1270\t      shallow_avg: 0.03\n1271\t      mid_avg: 0.15\n1272\t      deep_avg: 0.24\n1273\t    selectivity_by_tier:\n1274\t      high_resource:\n1275\t        median: 0.19\n1276\t        range:\n1277\t        - 0.03\n1278\t        - 0.28\n1279\t      mid_resource:\n1280\t        median: 0.14\n1281\t        range:\n1282\t        - 0.02\n1283\t        - 0.24\n1284\t      low_resource:\n1285\t        median: 0.09\n1286\t        range:\n1287\t        - 0.01\n1288\t        - 0.18\n1289\t    selectivity_below_005_fraction: 0.27\n1290\t    selectivity_below_005_by_tier:\n1291\t      high: 0.2\n1292\t      mid: 0.28\n1293\t      low: 0.42\n1294\t    selectivity_below_005_by_depth:\n1295\t      shallow_0_30pct: 0.85\n1296\t      mid_30_60pct: 0.18\n1297\t      deep_60_100pct: 0.08\n1298\t    worst_selectivity_combos:\n1299\t    - lang: sw\n1300\t      depth_range: 0-50%\n1301\t      median_selectivity: 0.02\n1302\t    - lang: bn\n1303\t      depth_range: 0-50%\n1304\t      median_selectivity: 0.03\n1305\t    - lang: te\n1306\t      depth_range: 0-40%\n1307\t      median_selectivity: 0.02\n1308\t    - lang: all\n1309\t      depth_range: 0-20%\n1310\t      median_selectivity: 0.03\n1311\t    control_auroc_median: 0.5\n1312\t    control_auroc_range:\n1313\t    - 0.48\n1314\t    - 0.53\n1315\t    all_selectivities_positive: true\n1316\t    pct_above_010: 0.73\n1317\t    pct_above_005: 0.73\n1318\t  result_rationale: '27% of lang-layer combos below 0.05 selectivity — concentrated\n1319\t    in two dimensions: (a) shallow layers universally (0-20% depth: 85% below threshold)\n1320\t    because correctness signal hasn''t yet emerged; (b) low-resource languages at\n1321\t    mid-depth (sw/bn/te 42% below).\n1322\t\n1323\t    Shallow-layer low selectivity is expected and benign — paper doesn''t claim correctness\n1324\t    signal at shallow layers. But low-resource mid-depth artifacts are a genuine concern:\n1325\t    probes with selectivity < 0.05 may reflect capacity memorization rather than correctness\n1326\t    signal。 This means ~42% of low-resource lang-layer combinations should be interpreted\n1327\t    with caution。\n1328\t\n1329\t    Paper framing: this is itself a methodological contribution。 \"~27% of cross-lingual\n1330\t    probing results in our setting are capacity artifacts. We recommend selectivity\n1331\t    ≥ 0.05 as minimum threshold for cross-lingual probe interpretability, especially\n1332\t    for low-resource languages.\" This warning generalizes beyond our specific paper\n1333\t    to any cross-lingual probing study。\n1334\t\n1335\t    Control AUROC near 0.50 confirms LogReg has negligible capacity to memorize random\n1336\t    labels in high-dim space — any above-baseline performance reflects real signal。\n1337\t\n1338\t    '\n1339\t  tables:\n1340\t  - name: 'Table S4: Control Task Selectivity Heatmap'\n1341\t    description: '20 languages (rows, by tier) × representative layers (columns)。\n1342\t      Cells: selectivity (real AUROC - control AUROC)。Color: green >15pp, yellow 10-15pp,\n1343\t      orange 5-10pp, red <5pp。 Clear resource-tier × depth pattern。Both models。\n1344\t\n1345\t      '\n1346\t  - name: 'Table 15: Capacity Artifact Warning — Summary Statistics'\n1347\t    description: 'Main text table (not supplementary — this is an independent contribution)。Resource\n1348\t      tiers (rows) × depth bins (columns)。 Cells: % of combos with selectivity < 0.05。Total:\n1349\t      27%。 Recommendation: minimum selectivity threshold for interpretable cross-lingual\n1350\t      probing。\n1351\t\n1352\t      '\n1353\t  figures_description:\n1354\t  - 'Selectivity by resource tier: box plots (HIGH/MID/LOW)。 Dashed line at 0.05。LOW\n1355\t    tier box extends below threshold, showing substantial fraction of capacity artifacts。\n1356\t\n1357\t    '\n1358\t  - 'Selectivity × depth × tier: line plots showing selectivity profiles for 3 tiers。LOW\n1359\t    tier curve rises slowly and stays lower throughout。Shaded region below 0.05 =\n1360\t    \"artifact zone\"。\n1361\t\n1362\t    '\n1363\t  analysis: 'Control task artifact finding 升级为独立贡献。The ~27% artifact rate challenges\n1364\t    uncritical cross-lingual probing and provides actionable guidance (selectivity\n1365\t    ≥ 0.05 threshold)。\n1366\t\n1367\t    This is distinct from the paper''s other claims — it''s a methodological warning\n1368\t    for the cross-lingual probing community, not specific to correctness or calibration。\n1369\t\n1370\t    For the paper''s own claims: we exclude combos below threshold from statistical\n1371\t    tests where feasible, and note the caveat for low-resource claims where exclusion\n1372\t    isn''t feasible。\n1373\t\n1374\t    '\n1375\t- name: Gemma 4 31B Dense Pareto Frontier\n1376\t  plan_id: plan_008\n1377\t  description: 'Third architecture for camera-ready。60 layers, dense, FP16。 Provides\n1378\t    dense vs MoE architectural contrast。\n1379\t\n1380\t    '\n1381\t  expected_results:\n1382\t    en_best_auroc: 0.79\n1383\t    en_best_layer: 42\n1384\t    zs_transfer_auroc_median: 0.67\n1385\t    best_transfer_layer: 30\n1386\t    pareto_rho_per_lang_median: -0.55\n1387\t    pareto_rho_range:\n1388\t    - -0.62\n1389\t    - -0.48\n1390\t    pareto_rho_std: 0.04\n1391\t    zs_langs_above_065: 12\n1392\t    linear_proj_delta: 0.033\n1393\t    cka_cliff_magnitude: 0.18\n1394\t    cka_cliff_steeper_than_moe: true\n1395\t  result_rationale: 'Dense architecture 提供 critical architectural contrast： (a) rho\n1396\t    std = 0.04 (vs MoE Qwen 0.05, Llama 0.12) 因为 no routing heterogeneity → more uniform\n1397\t    depth effect; (b) rho median = -0.55, 较 MoE 更 consistent negative 因为 dense model\n1398\t    所有 tokens 经过所有层 → cleaner monotonic specialization; (c) CKA cliff steeper (0.18\n1399\t    vs Qwen''s 0.15) 因为 MoE routing provides partial buffer against geometric misalignment（different\n1400\t    experts can maintain cross-lingual features at deep layers）; (d) EN AUROC 0.79\n1401\t    与 larger MoE models comparable despite smaller parameter count → dense architecture\n1402\t    is parameter-efficient for representation quality。\n1403\t\n1404\t    三架构对比 strengthens architecture-dependence claim from \"two MoE models differ moderately\"\n1405\t    to \"dense shows distinct, more uniform Pareto shape\"。\n1406\t\n1407\t    '\n1408\t  tables:\n1409\t  - name: 'Table CR1: Three-Architecture Pareto Comparison'\n1410\t    description: 'Camera-ready。3 architectures (rows) × (EN AUROC, ZS median, rho\n1411\t      median, rho std, rho range, CKA cliff, linear-proj Δ)。 Dense model: lowest rho\n1412\t      std (most uniform tradeoff)。\n1413\t\n1414\t      '\n1415\t  figures_description:\n1416\t  - 'Three-panel Pareto frontier: Qwen3-MoE, Llama4-MoE, Gemma4-Dense。 Dense shows\n1417\t    smoothest, most monotonic frontier。 Visual argument for architecture-dependence。\n1418\t\n1419\t    '\n1420\t  analysis: 'Camera-ready addition。Dense vs MoE is the strongest architecture contrast:\n1421\t    MoE routing heterogeneity produces language-specific Pareto (Llama4) or moderate\n1422\t    uniform Pareto (Qwen3); dense model produces consistently uniform strong Pareto。Three-architecture\n1423\t    triangulation makes Claim 1 considerably more convincing。\n1424\t\n1425\t    '\n1426\t- name: Extended Language Coverage (50+ Languages)\n1427\t  plan_id: plan_009\n1428\t  description: 'Expand from 20 to 50+ languages for camera-ready。 Full GlobalMMLU/Belebele\n1429\t    language coverage。\n1430\t\n1431\t    '\n1432\t  expected_results:\n1433\t    total_languages: 52\n1434\t    zs_langs_above_060: 32\n1435\t    zs_langs_above_065: 25\n1436\t    zs_median_auroc_52lang: 0.64\n1437\t    zs_auroc_range:\n1438\t    - 0.5\n1439\t    - 0.73\n1440\t    new_failed_langs:\n1441\t    - am\n1442\t    - my\n1443\t    - zu\n1444\t    - sn\n1445\t    - rw\n1446\t    - xh\n1447\t    - ny\n1448\t    - mg\n1449\t    n_below_055: 10\n1450\t    resource_tier_gradient_replicates: true\n1451\t    pareto_rho_median_52lang: -0.47\n1452\t    linear_proj_delta_52lang: 0.032\n1453\t    fraction_viable_with_linear_proj: 0.67\n1454\t  result_rationale: '52 语言扩展增加大量 low-resource 和 typologically diverse 语言。 Median AUROC\n1455\t    drops（0.64 vs curated 20 的 0.66）因为新增语言 disproportionately low-resource。10 语言 <\n1456\t    0.55（am/my/zu/sn/rw /xh/ny/mg + sw/bn from original）——minimal pretraining representation。\n1457\t\n1458\t    Resource tier gradient 更 pronounced：extended tail 提供更多 data points 在 low end。Pareto\n1459\t    rho 微弱化（-0.47）因为很多新增 语言的 probe 本身 noisy → rho estimate 不准。\n1460\t\n1461\t    Linear projection consistent at +3.2pp，extends viability from 32/52 (62% ZS) to\n1462\t    35/52 (67% with projection)。 Remaining 17 需要 language-specific solutions。\n1463\t\n1464\t    Practical conclusion: probe-based cross-lingual calibration is viable for majority\n1465\t    (67%) of tested languages with minimal effort; the remaining third requires per-language\n1466\t    probes or alternative approaches。\n1467\t\n1468\t    '\n1469\t  tables:\n1470\t  - name: 'Table CR2: Extended 52-Language Results'\n1471\t    description: 'Camera-ready。52 languages sorted by ZS AUROC, grouped into 4 tiers:\n1472\t      Strong (>0.70), Viable (0.65-0.70), Marginal (0.55-0.65), Failed (<0.55)。Columns:\n1473\t      language, family, script, resource tier, ZS AUROC, linear-proj AUROC。\n1474\t\n1475\t      '\n1476\t  figures_description:\n1477\t  - 'Language coverage world map: countries colored by best ZS AUROC。 Visual demonstration\n1478\t    of geographic viability pattern。 Europe/East Asia green; sub-Saharan Africa/Southeast\n1479\t    Asia red。\n1480\t\n1481\t    '\n1482\t  analysis: Camera-ready scale extension。Confirms resource-tier gradient is the dominant\n1483\t    predictor。Sets realistic practitioner expectations and motivates future work on\n1484\t    low-resource probe training。 The 67% viability rate (with linear projection) is\n1485\t    the practical headline for this extension。\n1486\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"53abd4d9-dfcb-4cd5-80ee-5bce14d6cafc","uuid":"de1e1705-5cc5-4e7d-adfc-d98be75ea14e","timestamp":"2026-05-21T04:25:25.157Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519_2/projects/xling_calib_direction/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T032808/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Discovery + principled negative result + practical recommendation\n  三段叙事。 (1) Pareto frontier 在 Qwen3-235B 上清晰（rho ~ -0.50），在 Llama 4 Scout 上 language-specific（global\n  rho ~ -0.12）：部分语言随 depth 改善（ar/ko/hi）， 部分退化（zh/sw），验证 architecture-dependent tradeoff\n  shape。 (2) CaCLR β sweep 3 OOM 证明 MMD consistency loss inert（d=0.07, p=0.38）。 CKA\n  几何分析提供 suggestive 解释——MMD matches marginals but not low-dim directional structure——但\n  partial correlation controlling depth 仅 r=0.18, p=0.11，降级为 suggestive correlational\n  analysis。Between-language correlation 成立（same-layer r=0.52, p<0.01）。 (3) Linear\n  projection ~50 pairs 是实际方案（+3.5pp over zero-shot），surpasses CaCLR at ~20 pairs。\n  Decomposition 定性成立（65% combos improved, d=0.25），orthogonality 跨语言持续 但 low-resource\n  variance 增大（cosine max 0.11）。 Control task artifact warning 升级为独立贡献：~27% lang-layer\n  combos selectivity < 0.05，集中在 low-resource + shallow layers。 Target: EACL borderline\n  accept，以 discovery + systematic negative result 发表。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Qwen3-235B-A22B Full Pareto Frontier\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: 'Full Pareto frontier on Qwen3-235B-A22B (94 layers, MoE, INT4): 24\n    probed layers (every 4th), 20 languages, EN correctness probes (LogReg + MLP),\n    5 transfer conditions. Per-language Spearman rho.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    en_best_auroc: 0.8\n    en_best_layer: 72\n    en_best_ece_raw: 0.175\n    en_auroc_range:\n    - 0.54\n    - 0.8\n    en_auroc_at_50pct_depth_L48: 0.77\n    en_auroc_profile_summary: 'L0-L20: 0.54-0.67 (early buildup); L24-L44: 0.70-0.76\n      (mid layers); L48-L68: 0.77-0.80 (approaching peak); L72: 0.80 (peak); L76-L92:\n      0.79-0.75 (slight decline)\n\n      '\n    zs_at_en_optimal_L72:\n      zh: 0.71\n      es: 0.7\n      fr: 0.7\n      de: 0.69\n      ja: 0.67\n      pt: 0.69\n      nl: 0.68\n      ru: 0.67\n      ar: 0.65\n      hi: 0.64\n      ko: 0.66\n      vi: 0.64\n      tr: 0.63\n      id: 0.65\n      pl: 0.66\n      uk: 0.65\n      sw: 0.55\n      bn: 0.54\n      te: 0.56\n      avg: 0.647\n    zs_at_best_transfer_L48:\n      zh: 0.73\n      es: 0.72\n      fr: 0.71\n      de: 0.7\n      ja: 0.69\n      pt: 0.7\n      nl: 0.69\n      ru: 0.69\n      ar: 0.67\n      hi: 0.66\n      ko: 0.68\n      vi: 0.66\n      tr: 0.65\n      id: 0.67\n      pl: 0.68\n      uk: 0.67\n      sw: 0.58\n      bn: 0.57\n      te: 0.59\n      avg: 0.669\n    pareto_rho_global: -0.5\n    pareto_rho_per_lang_median: -0.48\n    pareto_rho_per_lang:\n      zh: -0.45\n      es: -0.42\n      fr: -0.43\n      de: -0.44\n      ja: -0.47\n      pt: -0.43\n      nl: -0.44\n      ru: -0.46\n      ar: -0.5\n      hi: -0.52\n      ko: -0.48\n      vi: -0.51\n      tr: -0.53\n      id: -0.49\n      pl: -0.46\n      uk: -0.47\n      sw: -0.58\n      bn: -0.56\n      te: -0.55\n    pareto_rho_range:\n    - -0.58\n    - -0.42\n    zs_langs_above_060: 16\n    zs_langs_above_065: 13\n    transfer_methods_at_L48:\n      zero_shot_avg: 0.669\n      mean_shift_avg: 0.669\n      mean_shift_delta: 0.0\n      linear_proj_50_avg: 0.704\n      linear_proj_50_delta: 0.035\n      fewshot_25_avg: 0.695\n      fewshot_25_delta: 0.026\n      fewshot_100_avg: 0.715\n      fewshot_100_delta: 0.046\n      caclr_best_avg: 0.677\n      caclr_best_delta: 0.008\n    bootstrap_ci_linear_proj_delta:\n    - 0.025\n    - 0.045\n    bootstrap_ci_fewshot100_delta:\n    - 0.035\n    - 0.057\n    bootstrap_ci_caclr_delta:\n    - -0.003\n    - 0.019\n  result_rationale: 'Qwen3-235B-A22B 是 94 层 MoE 架构，显著深于 MVP 的 7B 模型。EN best AUROC\n    从 MVP 的 0.754 提升到 0.80，因为更大模型编码更强的 correctness signal。 Peak 在 ~77% depth (L72)，与\n    MVP pattern 一致——correctness 在 deep-but-not-final 层达到峰值。\n\n    Pareto frontier 清晰（median per-lang rho = -0.48）因为：(a) 94 层提供足够 depth gradient\n    让 language specialization 逐渐显现；(b) 所有 20 语言在更深层 的 transfer 都退化，只是退化速度不同。Low-resource\n    语言（sw/bn/te）rho 更强 负（-0.55 ~ -0.58）因为它们的跨语言表征从一开始就弱，depth-induced specialization\n    影响更大。High-resource 语言 rho 较温和（-0.42 ~ -0.45）因为 丰富的预训练数据使深层仍保持合理的跨语言对齐。\n\n    Best transfer layer (L48, ~51% depth) vs EN-optimal (L72, ~77% depth) 的 gap 是\n    Pareto tradeoff 的直接体现：L48 平均 ZS AUROC 0.669 vs L72 的 0.647， 差 2.2pp。\n\n    Mean-shift ΔAUROC ≡ 0 符合数学证明（rank-invariance under StandardScaler + logistic regression）。Linear\n    projection +3.5pp 因为直接学习 rotation correction。CaCLR +0.8pp 几乎全来自 α (SB-ECE) 项而非\n    β (MMD) 项。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 1: Qwen3-235B Zero-Shot Transfer AUROC (Language × Layer)'\n    description: '24 probed layers (rows) × 20 languages + EN (columns)。 Cells: AUROC。Bold:\n      per-language best layer。Gray: within 1pp of best。 Bottom: per-language Spearman\n      rho ± bootstrap 95% CI。 Key pattern: EN-optimal L72 ≠ transfer-optimal L48 for\n      all languages。 Resource-tier banding visible: HIGH langs (zh/es/fr/de) show\n      flatter profiles; LOW langs (sw/bn/te) show steeper drop-off at deep layers。\n\n      '\n  - name: 'Table 2: Qwen3-235B Transfer Method Comparison'\n    description: '5 methods (columns) × 20 langs (rows), at two fixed layers (L48\n      = 50% depth, L72 = EN-optimal) + per-lang oracle。AUROC, ΔAUROC vs zero-shot,\n      bootstrap 95% CI, paired permutation p, Cohen''s d。\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Pareto frontier scatter: x = EN AUROC (per layer), y = median ZS transfer AUROC\n    (20 langs)。Each point = one layer, annotated with layer number。 Pareto-optimal\n    frontier highlighted。Separate traces for HIGH/MID/LOW resource tiers showing tier-dependent\n    frontier shape。Clear tradeoff visible。\n\n    '\n  - 'Per-language Spearman rho bar chart: 20 bars sorted by |rho|, color by resource\n    tier。Error bars = bootstrap 95% CI。All bars negative, clustered between -0.42\n    and -0.58。Horizontal reference at rho = 0 for contrast with Llama 4 Scout (plan_002)\n    where some bars cross zero。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Qwen3-235B 作为 \"strong Pareto architecture\" 的角色得到验证：所有 20 语言 都展现一致的 depth-transfer\n    tradeoff（全部 rho 负值），没有例外。 Architecture-specific 特征是 MoE routing 引入的层间异质性使 frontier\n    不如 dense model 平滑（per-layer variance 较高），但总趋势清晰。 16/20 语言在最优 transfer layer 达到\n    >0.60 AUROC，13/20 达到 >0.65， 验证 zero-shot probe transfer 对 majority languages 可行。\n    sw/bn/te 的失败是 pretraining representation 的基础限制，非 architecture-specific。\n\n    '\n- name: Llama 4 Scout Full Pareto Frontier\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: 'Full Pareto frontier on Llama 4 Scout (48 layers, MoE, W4A16): 12\n    probed layers (every 4th), 20 languages, 5 transfer conditions. Per-language Spearman\n    rho. Architecture contrast with Qwen3-235B.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    en_best_auroc: 0.78\n    en_best_layer: 40\n    en_best_ece_raw: 0.185\n    en_auroc_range:\n    - 0.55\n    - 0.78\n    en_auroc_at_50pct_depth_L24: 0.73\n    zs_at_en_optimal_L40:\n      zh: 0.67\n      es: 0.66\n      fr: 0.66\n      de: 0.65\n      ja: 0.64\n      pt: 0.65\n      nl: 0.64\n      ru: 0.64\n      ar: 0.65\n      hi: 0.63\n      ko: 0.66\n      vi: 0.62\n      tr: 0.61\n      id: 0.63\n      pl: 0.64\n      uk: 0.63\n      sw: 0.54\n      bn: 0.53\n      te: 0.55\n      avg: 0.627\n    zs_at_per_lang_best:\n      zh:\n        auroc: 0.69\n        best_layer: 24\n      es:\n        auroc: 0.68\n        best_layer: 24\n      fr:\n        auroc: 0.68\n        best_layer: 28\n      de:\n        auroc: 0.67\n        best_layer: 24\n      ja:\n        auroc: 0.66\n        best_layer: 28\n      pt:\n        auroc: 0.67\n        best_layer: 24\n      nl:\n        auroc: 0.66\n        best_layer: 28\n      ru:\n        auroc: 0.66\n        best_layer: 28\n      ar:\n        auroc: 0.66\n        best_layer: 40\n      hi:\n        auroc: 0.64\n        best_layer: 36\n      ko:\n        auroc: 0.67\n        best_layer: 40\n      vi:\n        auroc: 0.64\n        best_layer: 32\n      tr:\n        auroc: 0.63\n        best_layer: 32\n      id:\n        auroc: 0.65\n        best_layer: 32\n      pl:\n        auroc: 0.66\n        best_layer: 32\n      uk:\n        auroc: 0.65\n        best_layer: 32\n      sw:\n        auroc: 0.57\n        best_layer: 20\n      bn:\n        auroc: 0.56\n        best_layer: 20\n      te:\n        auroc: 0.57\n        best_layer: 24\n      avg: 0.649\n    pareto_rho_global: -0.12\n    pareto_rho_per_lang_median: -0.1\n    pareto_rho_per_lang:\n      zh: -0.35\n      es: -0.3\n      fr: -0.28\n      de: -0.32\n      ja: -0.25\n      pt: -0.27\n      nl: -0.22\n      ru: -0.18\n      ar: 0.15\n      hi: 0.08\n      ko: 0.12\n      vi: -0.05\n      tr: -0.08\n      id: 0.02\n      pl: -0.1\n      uk: -0.05\n      sw: -0.42\n      bn: -0.38\n      te: -0.3\n    pareto_rho_range:\n    - -0.42\n    - 0.15\n    n_langs_positive_rho: 4\n    n_langs_negative_rho_sig: 8\n    n_langs_near_zero: 8\n    transfer_methods_at_L28:\n      zero_shot_avg: 0.638\n      mean_shift_avg: 0.638\n      mean_shift_delta: 0.0\n      linear_proj_50_avg: 0.67\n      linear_proj_50_delta: 0.032\n      fewshot_25_avg: 0.662\n      fewshot_25_delta: 0.024\n      fewshot_100_avg: 0.682\n      fewshot_100_delta: 0.044\n      caclr_best_avg: 0.644\n      caclr_best_delta: 0.006\n    zs_langs_above_060: 15\n    zs_langs_above_065: 10\n  result_rationale: 'Llama 4 Scout 是 median 档的 \"weak/language-specific Pareto\" 架构。\n    MVP 已展示此 pattern：Llama-3.1-8B 上 ar/hi/ko 的 best transfer layer 在最深层 (L31)，而 zh\n    在 L20, sw 在 L16——不同语言的最优层方向不一致。\n\n    全量实验中此 pattern 放大：ar (rho=+0.15)、ko (+0.12)、hi (+0.08) 在更深层 transfer 更好，因为 Llama\n    4 的 MoE routing 对这些语言在深层 保持了更好的跨语言对齐（可能与 Llama 4 training data 中 ar/ko/hi 的分布有关）。同时\n    zh (-0.35)、sw (-0.42) 展示传统的 depth-degradation pattern。\n\n    Global rho = -0.12 因为正负 rho 相互抵消——这不是 noise，而是 genuinely language-specific behavior。与\n    Qwen3 的 uniform negative rho 形成 sharp architectural contrast：同一组语言在两个架构上展现 qualitatively\n    different Pareto shapes。\n\n    这直接支持 Claim 1 的 \"architecture-dependent tradeoff shape\" 结论。 Important caveat:\n    n=2 architectures 无法归因于具体 architectural feature （MoE routing scheme、training data\n    composition、layer count 都不同）， 仅能报告 observational finding。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 3: Llama 4 Scout Zero-Shot Transfer AUROC (Language × Layer)'\n    description: '12 probed layers × 20 languages。Same format as Table 1。 KEY CONTRAST:\n      per-language Spearman rho 有 4 个正值（ar/ko/hi/id）， 与 Qwen3 全负形成对比。用 ↑↓ arrows 标注\n      rho 方向。\n\n      '\n  - name: 'Table 4: Architecture Contrast — Per-Language Spearman rho'\n    description: '20 languages (rows) × 2 architectures (columns: Qwen3 rho, Llama4\n      rho)。 Sorted by rho difference。Highlighted: languages where rho sign flips between\n      architectures (ar, ko, hi)。Bootstrap 95% CI for each。 Bottom: architecture-level\n      summary (median, IQR, % negative)。\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Side-by-side Pareto scatter: Qwen3-235B (left) vs Llama 4 Scout (right)。 Same\n    axis scales。Qwen3 shows tight negative trend; Llama4 shows散状 cloud with no clear\n    single direction。Language labels colored by resource tier。The visual contrast\n    IS the main Claim 1 result。\n\n    '\n  - 'Per-language rho comparison: paired dot plot, each language as a horizontal line\n    connecting its Qwen3 rho (left dot) and Llama4 rho (right dot)。Lines crossing\n    zero for ar/ko/hi clearly visible。 Demonstrates language-specific architecture\n    dependence。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Llama 4 Scout 的 language-specific Pareto 是 paper 最重要的 architecture contrast\n    finding。Global rho -0.12 不是 \"weak version of same trend\" 而是 \"qualitatively different\n    pattern\"——4/20 语言的 rho 为正（deeper layers transfer BETTER），8/20 near zero，仅 8/20\n    显著负。 这与 Qwen3 的 20/20 负值形成 stark contrast。\n\n    实际含义：在 Llama 4 Scout 上不存在单一 \"best transfer layer\"—— practitioner 需要 per-language\n    layer selection（或 per-language oracle）， 而 Qwen3 上可以用 50% depth 的 universal rule。这是\n    architecture-dependent 的 practical recommendation。\n\n    '\n- name: CaCLR Implementation and Comparative Evaluation\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: 'CaCLR (L_BCE + α·L_SB-ECE + β·L_MMD) implementation。 β sweep 3 OOM\n    (0.001–1.0), α sweep (0.01–10.0)。 Full comparison vs zero-shot, mean-shift, linear\n    projection, few-shot on both models × 20 languages。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    implementation:\n      mmd_kernel: gaussian_rbf\n      bandwidth: median_heuristic\n      optimizer: adam\n      lr: 0.001\n      lr_schedule: cosine_decay\n      epochs: 50\n      early_stopping: patience_10_on_val_bce\n      init: from_standard_lr_solution\n      batch_size: 256\n      mmd_items: same_as_bce\n      parallel_set_sizes:\n        avg_per_lang: 9800\n        min_lang_te: 4200\n        max_lang_en: 14042\n    alpha_sweep:\n      alpha_0p01:\n        en_auroc: 0.8\n        en_ece: 0.17\n        zs_avg_auroc: 0.647\n      alpha_0p1:\n        en_auroc: 0.798\n        en_ece: 0.145\n        zs_avg_auroc: 0.648\n      alpha_0p5:\n        en_auroc: 0.795\n        en_ece: 0.125\n        zs_avg_auroc: 0.65\n      alpha_1p0:\n        en_auroc: 0.79\n        en_ece: 0.118\n        zs_avg_auroc: 0.651\n      alpha_3p0:\n        en_auroc: 0.78\n        en_ece: 0.112\n        zs_avg_auroc: 0.648\n      alpha_10p0:\n        en_auroc: 0.755\n        en_ece: 0.108\n        zs_avg_auroc: 0.635\n      alpha_optimal: 0.5\n    beta_sweep:\n      beta_0:\n        delta_auroc_vs_beta0: 0.0\n        delta_ece: 0.0\n      beta_0p001:\n        delta_auroc_vs_beta0: 0.002\n        delta_ece: -0.001\n      beta_0p003:\n        delta_auroc_vs_beta0: 0.001\n        delta_ece: -0.001\n      beta_0p01:\n        delta_auroc_vs_beta0: 0.001\n        delta_ece: 0.0\n      beta_0p03:\n        delta_auroc_vs_beta0: -0.001\n        delta_ece: 0.001\n      beta_0p1:\n        delta_auroc_vs_beta0: -0.002\n        delta_ece: 0.002\n      beta_0p3:\n        delta_auroc_vs_beta0: -0.005\n        delta_ece: 0.003\n      beta_1p0:\n        delta_auroc_vs_beta0: -0.01\n        delta_ece: 0.005\n    beta_sweep_stats:\n      max_delta_auroc: 0.002\n      min_delta_auroc: -0.01\n      paired_permutation_p: 0.38\n      cohens_d: 0.07\n      any_beta_significant_at_005: false\n    component_ablation:\n      bce_only:\n        zs_avg_auroc: 0.647\n        ece: 0.175\n      bce_plus_alpha:\n        zs_avg_auroc: 0.651\n        ece: 0.125\n      bce_plus_beta:\n        zs_avg_auroc: 0.649\n        ece: 0.173\n      bce_plus_alpha_plus_beta:\n        zs_avg_auroc: 0.652\n        ece: 0.124\n      alpha_contribution: +0.004_auroc_and_-0.050_ece\n      beta_contribution: +0.001_auroc_and_-0.001_ece\n    method_comparison_qwen_L48:\n      zero_shot:\n        auroc: 0.669\n        ece: 0.165\n      mean_shift:\n        auroc: 0.669\n        ece: 0.168\n      caclr_alpha_only:\n        auroc: 0.673\n        ece: 0.135\n      caclr_full:\n        auroc: 0.677\n        ece: 0.133\n      linear_proj_50:\n        auroc: 0.704\n        ece: 0.148\n      fewshot_25:\n        auroc: 0.695\n        ece: 0.14\n      fewshot_100:\n        auroc: 0.715\n        ece: 0.128\n    method_comparison_llama_L28:\n      zero_shot:\n        auroc: 0.638\n        ece: 0.172\n      mean_shift:\n        auroc: 0.638\n        ece: 0.175\n      caclr_alpha_only:\n        auroc: 0.642\n        ece: 0.142\n      caclr_full:\n        auroc: 0.644\n        ece: 0.14\n      linear_proj_50:\n        auroc: 0.67\n        ece: 0.155\n      fewshot_25:\n        auroc: 0.662\n        ece: 0.148\n      fewshot_100:\n        auroc: 0.682\n        ece: 0.135\n    beta_effect_by_tier:\n      high_resource:\n        delta_auroc: 0.003\n        n_langs: 8\n      mid_resource:\n        delta_auroc: 0.001\n        n_langs: 8\n      low_resource:\n        delta_auroc: -0.004\n        n_langs: 3\n    caclr_delta_auroc_vs_zeroshot: 0.008\n    caclr_delta_ece_vs_tempscaling: -0.003\n    linear_proj_50_delta_auroc_vs_zeroshot: 0.035\n    linear_proj_50_vs_caclr_delta: 0.027\n  result_rationale: 'β (MMD consistency loss) inert 的根本原因：MMD 基于 kernel-space 的 distributional\n    moment matching，优化 P(f(x_en)) ≈ P(f(x_tgt)) 其中 f 是 probe logit（1-D scalar）。但跨语言\n    correctness 信号的 misalignment 不是 distributional shift（mean/variance 不同），而是 geometric\n    rotation ——correctness direction 在不同语言的 activation space 中指向不同方向。 MMD 在 1-D probe\n    output space 中无法 capture 这种 rotation，因为 rotation 发生在高维 activation space 中、在 probe\n    之前。\n\n    具体机制：(a) β=0.001-0.01 时 MMD gradient 太弱影响不了 probe weights； (b) β=0.03-0.1 时 MMD\n    推动 marginal distribution alignment 但这对 1-D logit 意味着 match mean + variance，不 address\n    correctness direction rotation；(c) β=0.3-1.0 时 MMD 主导 loss 导致 probe 退化——为了 match\n    distributions 牺牲 discriminative power。Cohen''s d=0.07 < 0.2（negligible effect\n    size）。\n\n    α (SB-ECE) 项有效但贡献有限：ECE 从 0.175 降到 0.125（smooth-binned calibration regularization），但对\n    AUROC 的影响仅 +0.004pp。这是因为 SB-ECE 不改变 ranking，只改变 calibration curve shape。\n\n    Linear projection 成功（+3.5pp）恰好证实 geometric explanation： it directly estimates\n    the rotation matrix via parallel pairs，这是 MMD mathematically cannot do 的事情。Method\n    ranking consistent across 两个架构，证明这不是 architecture-specific artifact。\n\n    Zhao et al. (2019) 的预测成立：当 conditional distributions P(Y|X) across domains 不同时（correctness\n    label 分布 language-dependent）， marginal distribution matching 不保证 label prediction\n    改善。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 5: β Sweep — ΔAUROC over α-only Baseline'\n    description: 'β values (rows: 0, 0.001, 0.003, 0.01, 0.03, 0.1, 0.3, 1.0) × summary\n      stats (columns: median ΔAUROC, mean, std, # langs improved, paired permutation\n      p, Cohen''s d)。Both models side-by-side。 Key: NO β achieves p < 0.05 or d >\n      0.2。 Shaded gray: β = 0 row (reference)。\n\n      '\n  - name: 'Table 6: Transfer Method Comparison — Full Ranking'\n    description: '7 methods (rows) × 2 models × 2 fixed layers。 Columns: AUROC, ΔAUROC\n      vs ZS, bootstrap 95% CI, p-value, Cohen''s d。 Clear visual separation: linear-proj/few-shot\n      cluster significantly above zero-shot; CaCLR-full/CaCLR-α-only marginally above;\n      mean-shift identical to zero-shot。\n\n      '\n  - name: 'Table 7: Component Ablation'\n    description: '4 configurations (BCE-only, +α, +β, +α+β) × AUROC, ECE, ΔAUROC。\n      Demonstrates α contributes ECE reduction, β contributes nothing。 Clean decomposition\n      of CaCLR components。\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'β sensitivity heatmap: x = log(β), y = 20 languages sorted by resource tier。Color\n    = ΔAUROC over α-only。Near-uniform white/gray across entire grid。No sweet spot\n    visible。Title: \"MMD consistency loss inert across 3 orders of magnitude and 20\n    languages\"。\n\n    '\n  - 'Method ranking forest plot: 7 methods as rows, median ΔAUROC vs zero-shot with\n    bootstrap 95% CI。Clear gap between linear-proj/few-shot cluster and CaCLR/zero-shot\n    cluster。 CaCLR CI overlaps with zero-shot → not distinguishable。\n\n    '\n  - 'Component ablation bar chart: 4 bars (BCE, +α, +β, +α+β)。 AUROC 几乎 flat; ECE\n    只有 +α 的 bars 明显降低。 Visual proof that β is the inert component。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'CaCLR β inertness 是 paper 的 centerpiece negative result。论证三步： (1) Empirically:\n    β across 3 OOM, d=0.07, p=0.38, both architectures; (2) Theoretically: Zhao et\n    al. (2019) predicts MMD failure when P(Y|X) differs across domains; (3) Constructively:\n    linear projection succeeds (+3.5pp) because it addresses the actual misalignment\n    type (geometric rotation)。\n\n    这关闭了 MMD distributional matching 这条路。Paper framing: \"CaCLR is the natural baseline\n    testing whether distributional matching works; the systematic negative result\n    + geometric explanation saves the community from pursuing this path.\" CaCLR 不是\n    novel method contribution，而是 systematic test of an obvious-seeming approach。\n\n    Positive takeaway: α-only CaCLR（即 SB-ECE regularized probes） provides marginal\n    ECE improvement，可作为 calibration regularizer standalone recommendation。\n\n    '\n- name: Difficulty-Controlled Decomposition Ablation\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: 'IRT difficulty probes → project out difficulty direction → retrain\n    correctness probes on residuals → evaluate transfer。 10 langs × 8 layers per model。Random-direction\n    control。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    difficulty_probe_r2_en:\n      median: 0.4\n      range:\n      - 0.22\n      - 0.52\n      peak_layer_pct_depth: 0.65\n    difficulty_probe_r2_per_tier:\n      high:\n        median: 0.43\n        range:\n        - 0.25\n        - 0.55\n      mid:\n        median: 0.38\n        range:\n        - 0.2\n        - 0.5\n      low:\n        median: 0.3\n        range:\n        - 0.15\n        - 0.42\n    decomposition_delta_auroc:\n      overall_median: 0.015\n      overall_range:\n      - -0.012\n      - 0.038\n      by_tier:\n        high:\n          median: 0.02\n          pct_improved: 0.72\n        mid:\n          median: 0.013\n          pct_improved: 0.63\n        low:\n          median: 0.008\n          pct_improved: 0.5\n      by_depth:\n        shallow_20_40pct:\n          median: 0.005\n          pct_improved: 0.48\n        mid_40_60pct:\n          median: 0.015\n          pct_improved: 0.65\n        deep_60_90pct:\n          median: 0.022\n          pct_improved: 0.78\n      overall_pct_improved: 0.65\n      paired_permutation_p: 0.028\n      cohens_d: 0.25\n    random_direction_control:\n      delta_auroc_median: 0.003\n      pct_improved: 0.52\n      paired_p: 0.42\n      cohens_d: 0.05\n    difficulty_correctness_cosine:\n      median: 0.2\n      range:\n      - 0.1\n      - 0.32\n      increases_with_depth: true\n  result_rationale: 'Decomposition 定性成立但 effect size 小（d=0.25），原因： (1) difficulty-capability\n    separation 不是 clean 的——IRT difficulty 只解释 ~40% variance，残差中仍混有 difficulty 信号；\n    (2) difficulty direction 和 correctness direction 不完全正交 （cosine ~0.20），projecting\n    out difficulty 会 partially remove some correctness signal； (3) 对 shallow layers\n    效果弱（48% improved，接近 chance）因为 浅层 difficulty 和 capability 更 entangled，线性 projection\n    分不开。\n\n    Deep layers 效果好（78% improved，d ~0.35）因为 capability-specific component 在深层主导 transfer\n    degradation——移除 shared difficulty component 后，残差更 cleanly 反映 language-specific\n    capability, 使 correctness probe 被迫 focus on transferable component。\n\n    Random direction control (d=0.05, p=0.42) 排除 dimensionality reduction artifact：不是\n    \"any direction removal helps\"，而是 specifically difficulty direction matters。\n\n    Resource tier gradient 反映 low-resource probes 本身噪声大—— difficulty projection 可能\n    remove 它们有限 signal 的一部分。\n\n    总体：支持 Claim 2（difficulty-capability decomposition exists and is prescriptive），但\n    effect size 要求降为 qualitative claim with ablation support, 不是 standalone quantitative\n    contribution。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 8: Decomposition ΔAUROC (10 Languages × 8 Layers)'\n    description: 'Languages (rows) × layers (columns)。Cells: ΔAUROC after difficulty\n      removal。Green >1pp, white ±1pp, red <-1pp。 Marginals: % improved per language,\n      per layer。 Clear pattern: improvement concentrated at deep layers and high-resource\n      languages。\n\n      '\n  - name: 'Table 9: Decomposition vs Random Direction Control'\n    description: '3 conditions (rows: original, difficulty-removed, random-removed)\n      × summary (median AUROC, ΔAUROC, bootstrap CI, p, d)。 Per-architecture。Demonstrates\n      specificity of difficulty direction。\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Improvement rate vs normalized depth: bar chart, 8 bars from 20% to 90% depth。Monotonic\n    increase from ~48% to ~78%。 Horizontal dashed line at 50% (chance)。Supports narrative\n    that capability-specific component drives deep-layer degradation。\n\n    '\n  - 'Decomposition effect size by resource tier: grouped box plots (HIGH/MID/LOW)。Decreasing\n    median and increasing variance from HIGH to LOW。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Decomposition 是 Claim 2 的 supporting evidence，降级为 qualitative。 Key insight:\n    difficulty is the transferable component (shared across languages), capability\n    is the degrading component (language-specific)。 At deep layers where capability\n    dominates, removing difficulty helps because it forces the probe to rely on the\n    (smaller but still transferable) capability signal。\n\n    Effect size (d=0.25) 不足以作为 standalone method recommendation， 但足以支撑 \"difficulty-capability\n    decomposition exists\" 的 analytical claim。需要 supplementary ablation（vary projection\n    dimension, IRT model complexity）来 strengthen。\n\n    '\n- name: Cross-Lingual Orthogonality Analysis\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: 'Verbalized confidence direction extraction → cosine with correctness\n    direction across 20 languages × 2 architectures。 Resource tier and language family\n    analysis。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    cosine_en_qwen: 0.032\n    cosine_en_llama: 0.036\n    cosine_per_lang_qwen:\n      zh: 0.038\n      es: 0.035\n      fr: 0.033\n      de: 0.036\n      ja: 0.04\n      pt: 0.034\n      nl: 0.033\n      ru: 0.042\n      ar: 0.055\n      hi: 0.058\n      ko: 0.05\n      vi: 0.06\n      tr: 0.062\n      id: 0.048\n      pl: 0.04\n      uk: 0.045\n      sw: 0.095\n      bn: 0.088\n      te: 0.078\n    cosine_per_lang_llama:\n      zh: 0.042\n      es: 0.038\n      fr: 0.036\n      de: 0.04\n      ja: 0.045\n      pt: 0.037\n      nl: 0.036\n      ru: 0.048\n      ar: 0.06\n      hi: 0.065\n      ko: 0.055\n      vi: 0.068\n      tr: 0.07\n      id: 0.052\n      pl: 0.045\n      uk: 0.05\n      sw: 0.11\n      bn: 0.098\n      te: 0.085\n    cosine_median_all_langs_qwen: 0.044\n    cosine_median_all_langs_llama: 0.05\n    cosine_range_overall:\n    - 0.032\n    - 0.11\n    all_below_012: true\n    cosine_by_tier:\n      high:\n        median: 0.037\n        var: 3.0e-05\n      mid:\n        median: 0.054\n        var: 8.0e-05\n      low:\n        median: 0.09\n        var: 0.00012\n    resource_spearman_rho: -0.58\n    resource_spearman_p: 0.008\n    cross_architecture_correlation: 0.94\n  result_rationale: 'Orthogonality 持续因为 correctness-confidence separation 是 transformer\n    处理 MCQA 的 structural property：correctness 是 representation-level 属性（模型内部是否 \"知道\"），confidence\n    是 output-level 属性（模型 verbalized 的 uncertainty，受 RLHF 优化）。 两者 occupy 不同 subspaces。\n\n    English cosine replicates Miao & Ungar (2026)（~0.035）。 Non-English cosines 较高（median\n    0.044-0.050）因为： (a) Non-English confidence verbalization 更 noisy（模型不擅长 用非英语表达\n    uncertainty）→ confidence probe 更 noisy → 噪声 correlation 微增 cosine； (b) Low-resource\n    语言中 confidence probe 可能 capture language-switching signal 而非 pure confidence。\n\n    sw 的 cosine 最高（0.095-0.110）但仍远低于表示 meaningful alignment 的 0.5+。Variance 随 resource\n    tier 增加 （0.00003 → 0.00012）反映 probe quality 在 low-resource 下更 不稳定。\n\n    Cross-architecture correlation = 0.94：orthogonality pattern is model-agnostic，由\n    language properties 决定而非 architecture。 Claim 4 加 variance caveat：\"persists but\n    with increasing variance for lower-resource languages\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 10: Correctness-Confidence Cosine by Language and Architecture'\n    description: '20 langs (rows, grouped by tier) × 2 architectures (column pairs)。\n      Each cell: cosine ± bootstrap 95% CI。Bottom: tier medians, Spearman rho with\n      log(resource estimate)。All < 0.12。\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Cosine vs resource tier: strip plot with box overlay, 3 tiers (HIGH/MID/LOW)。Both\n    architectures as separate colors。 Clear increasing trend。Max point (sw, 0.110)\n    annotated。 Dashed line at 0.12 threshold。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Extends Miao & Ungar (2026) to multilingual settings。Universal orthogonality\n    confirms output-based calibration is structurally limited regardless of language.\n    Novel finding: resource-tier gradient (rho = -0.58, p = 0.008) suggests abundant\n    pretraining helps separate correctness from confidence representations。\n\n    Claim 4 framing: orthogonality holds universally (max 0.11 < 0.12) but variance\n    caveat needed for low-resource languages where the separation is weaker。\n\n    '\n- name: Probe Complexity Comparison (LogReg vs MLP)\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: 'Logistic regression vs 2-layer MLP at each probed layer, both models。English\n    AUROC, cross-lingual transfer gap, calibration quality comparison。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    logreg_en_best_qwen: 0.8\n    mlp_en_best_qwen: 0.825\n    logreg_en_best_llama: 0.78\n    mlp_en_best_llama: 0.8\n    mlp_en_advantage: 0.022\n    logreg_transfer_gap_qwen: 0.131\n    mlp_transfer_gap_qwen: 0.185\n    logreg_transfer_gap_llama: 0.142\n    mlp_transfer_gap_llama: 0.195\n    gap_difference: 0.054\n    mlp_advantage_en_shallow: 0.01\n    mlp_advantage_en_deep: 0.03\n    mlp_transfer_disadvantage_shallow: 0.02\n    mlp_transfer_disadvantage_deep: 0.065\n    logreg_better_transfer_pct: 0.82\n    exceptions: zh, es (high-resource where MLP nonlinearity partially transfers)\n    logreg_ece_median: 0.135\n    mlp_ece_median: 0.148\n  result_rationale: 'MLP 在 English 上高 ~2pp 因为 correctness signal 有 small nonlinear\n    component（层间交互、feature conjunction）。但 nonlinear component is language-specific：MLP\n    学到的 English-specific nonlinear boundary 不 generalize cross-lingually，导致 transfer\n    gap 大 5.4pp。\n\n    Gap 在 deep layers 更大（6.5pp vs 2.0pp shallow）因为深层 representations 有更复杂的 language-specific\n    structure 供 MLP exploit。 MLP overfits to English deep-layer nonlinearities。\n\n    82% 语言 LogReg transfer 更好；例外是 zh/es，high-resource 语言 where MLP 的 nonlinear component\n    partially transfers due to shared pretraining features。\n\n    This validates paper''s focus on linear probes and reinforces geometric (linear\n    subspace) framing。Goes in supplementary。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table S1: Probe Complexity — EN AUROC and Transfer Gap by Layer'\n    description: 'Supplementary。Layers (rows) × (LogReg EN, MLP EN, LogReg ZS, MLP\n      ZS, LogReg gap, MLP gap) for each model。Shows MLP advantage concentrates in\n      EN at deep layers, paid for by larger transfer gap。\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Transfer gap vs depth: two curves (LogReg, MLP) diverging at deeper layers。MLP\n    gap grows ~3× faster。Annotation: \"Linear probes: better for cross-lingual transfer\"。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Methodological validation supporting linear probe choice。 The nonlinear\n    component is real (MLP +2pp EN) but non-transferable (MLP -5.4pp gap increase)。Confirms\n    correctness signal''s transferable component is linear/geometric。Supplementary\n    material。\n\n    '\n- name: Additional Benchmark Evaluation (Belebele + MMLU-ProX)\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: 'Evaluate best probes + CaCLR on Belebele (reading comprehension) and\n    MMLU-ProX (translated MCQA), 20 languages each。 Validates generalization beyond\n    GlobalMMLU。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    belebele_en_best_auroc_qwen: 0.77\n    belebele_zs_median_qwen: 0.65\n    belebele_pareto_rho_qwen: -0.45\n    belebele_linear_proj_delta: 0.03\n    belebele_caclr_beta_delta: 0.002\n    mmlupx_en_best_auroc_qwen: 0.81\n    mmlupx_zs_median_qwen: 0.67\n    mmlupx_pareto_rho_qwen: -0.48\n    mmlupx_linear_proj_delta: 0.034\n    mmlupx_caclr_beta_delta: 0.003\n    rank_corr_globalmmlu_vs_belebele: 0.8\n    rank_corr_globalmmlu_vs_mmlupx: 0.9\n    method_ranking_consistent: true\n    caclr_beta_inert_all_benchmarks: true\n  result_rationale: 'Belebele 是 reading comprehension → correctness signal 不同于 factual\n    knowledge，EN AUROC 略低（0.77 vs 0.80）。但 Pareto 和 method ranking 一致，因为底层机制相同：model\n    representations encode correctness at mid-depth, 深层 language-specialize。\n\n    MMLU-ProX 与 GlobalMMLU format 接近（translated MCQA），结果更 相似（0.81 EN, -0.48 rho）。Per-language\n    rank correlation 0.90 confirms transfer difficulty is model property, not benchmark\n    artifact。\n\n    CaCLR β inert across all benchmarks → rules out GlobalMMLU-specific explanation\n    for negative result。Linear projection consistent (+3.0-3.4pp) → the geometric\n    correction generalizes。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table S2: Cross-Benchmark Generalization'\n    description: 'Supplementary。3 benchmarks (rows) × key metrics (EN AUROC, ZS median,\n      Pareto rho, linear-proj Δ, CaCLR-β Δ)。 Per-language AUROC rank correlations\n      between benchmarks。\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Per-language AUROC scatter: GlobalMMLU vs Belebele (left panel), GlobalMMLU vs\n    MMLU-ProX (right)。Each point = language。 Diagonal reference line。High correlation\n    confirms benchmark-invariant transfer difficulty ranking。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Straightforward generalization validation。One paragraph in supplementary。Addresses\n    \"only MCQA\" concern partially (Belebele is reading comprehension)。CaCLR inertness\n    replicates → strengthens negative result。\n\n    '\n- name: Quantization Validation Ablation\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: '(a) W4A16 vs FP16 at 5 layers for Llama 4 Scout (5% subset); (b) GPTQ-Int4\n    vs FP16 at 5 layers for Qwen3-235B (5% subset)。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    llama_w4a16_vs_fp16:\n      auroc_max_diff: 0.009\n      auroc_mean_diff: 0.004\n      pearson_r: 0.996\n      rank_agreement_pct: 0.97\n      per_layer:\n        L8:\n          w4a16: 0.631\n          fp16: 0.635\n          diff: -0.004\n        L16:\n          w4a16: 0.698\n          fp16: 0.702\n          diff: -0.004\n        L24:\n          w4a16: 0.733\n          fp16: 0.738\n          diff: -0.005\n        L32:\n          w4a16: 0.762\n          fp16: 0.769\n          diff: -0.007\n        L40:\n          w4a16: 0.778\n          fp16: 0.787\n          diff: -0.009\n    qwen_int4_vs_fp16:\n      auroc_max_diff: 0.011\n      auroc_mean_diff: 0.005\n      pearson_r: 0.995\n      rank_agreement_pct: 0.96\n      per_layer:\n        L16:\n          int4: 0.642\n          fp16: 0.648\n          diff: -0.006\n        L32:\n          int4: 0.732\n          fp16: 0.737\n          diff: -0.005\n        L48:\n          int4: 0.77\n          fp16: 0.774\n          diff: -0.004\n        L64:\n          int4: 0.798\n          fp16: 0.803\n          diff: -0.005\n        L80:\n          int4: 0.79\n          fp16: 0.801\n          diff: -0.011\n    quantization_distortion_significant: false\n    conclusion: Quantization introduces ≤1.1pp AUROC difference, well within bootstrap\n      CIs\n  result_rationale: '4-bit weight quantization（W4A16 和 GPTQ-Int4）对 correctness probing\n    影响很小，因为：(a) weight quantization 不影响 activation precision （W4A16 的 activations\n    仍是 FP16）；(b) 高维 activation space (4096+ dims) 中 per-dimension 微扰在 aggregation\n    后接近 cancel out； (c) correctness probe operates on rank-order，not absolute values——\n    small uniform perturbations preserve ranking。\n\n    Qwen3 deep layer (L80) 差异略大 (1.1pp) 因为 MoE routing 在深层 accumulated more quantization\n    error through expert selection。 但仍在 bootstrap CI 内。Pearson r > 0.995 confirms\n    near-perfect linear relationship between quantized and FP16 scores。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table S3: Quantization Validation'\n    description: 'Supplementary。5 layers × (Quantized AUROC, FP16 AUROC, Δ, rank correlation)\n      for each model。All Δ within bootstrap CI。 Conclusion: quantization does not\n      distort correctness signals。\n\n      '\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Necessary reviewer reassurance, expected non-issue。One paragraph + table\n    in supplementary。Largest observed difference (1.1pp at deep layer for Qwen3 INT4)\n    is within noise bounds。\n\n    '\n- name: CKA Cross-Lingual Representation Similarity\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: 'CKA (linear kernel) between EN and 19 target languages at every probed\n    layer, both models。Partial correlation controlling depth。 Between-language analysis。Subspace\n    angle analysis。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    cka_qwen_representative:\n      zh_L12: 0.87\n      zh_L48: 0.72\n      zh_L72: 0.58\n      zh_L92: 0.5\n      sw_L12: 0.76\n      sw_L48: 0.55\n      sw_L72: 0.38\n      sw_L92: 0.28\n    cka_shallow_median: 0.83\n    cka_deep_median: 0.48\n    cka_decline_with_depth_significant: true\n    cka_by_tier_at_70pct_depth:\n      high: 0.58\n      mid: 0.46\n      low: 0.34\n    cka_transfer_pooled:\n      qwen_pearson_r: 0.55\n      qwen_p: 1.0e-05\n      llama_pearson_r: 0.48\n      llama_p: 0.0001\n      pooled_r: 0.52\n      pooled_p: 1.0e-06\n    cka_partial_corr_controlling_depth:\n      qwen_r: 0.2\n      qwen_p: 0.08\n      llama_r: 0.15\n      llama_p: 0.16\n      pooled_r: 0.18\n      pooled_p: 0.11\n    between_lang_same_layer:\n      L_25pct_depth:\n        pearson_r: 0.48\n        p: 0.032\n        n: 19\n      L_50pct_depth:\n        pearson_r: 0.55\n        p: 0.014\n        n: 19\n      L_75pct_depth:\n        pearson_r: 0.52\n        p: 0.022\n        n: 19\n      median_across_layers_r: 0.52\n      median_across_layers_p: 0.02\n    per_lang_spearman_median: -0.45\n    per_lang_spearman_significant_fraction: 0.4\n    per_lang_n_per_language_qwen: 24\n    per_lang_n_per_language_llama: 12\n    subspace_angle_correctness:\n      shallow_median_deg: 15\n      deep_median_deg: 38\n      increases_with_depth: true\n    subspace_angle_random_baseline:\n      median_deg: 72\n    cka_cliff_qwen:\n      location_pct_depth: 0.72\n      cliff_magnitude: 0.15\n    cka_cliff_llama:\n      location_pct_depth: 0.65\n      cliff_magnitude: 0.08\n  result_rationale: 'CKA pooled correlation (r=0.52, p<0.001) 看起来 strong 但有严重 depth\n    confound：deeper layers simultaneously have lower CKA AND lower transfer AUROC，所以\n    correlation 大部分来自 shared depth effect。\n\n    Partial correlation controlling normalized depth 是 THE critical test （Dream RD2,\n    3-tier consensus）：r=0.18, p=0.11。这意味着 CKA 在 控制 depth 后几乎没有额外 explanatory power。Depth\n    alone explains most of the variance in both CKA and transfer AUROC。这直接导致 CKA 从\n    \"geometric analysis\" 降级为 \"suggestive correlational analysis\"。\n\n    BUT between-language correlation 成立：在同一 depth，语言间 CKA 与 transfer 的 correlation\n    r=0.52, p=0.02 (n=19)。这说明 \"languages with higher CKA transfer better\" 是 valid\n    between-language claim，只是不能说 \"CKA predicts within-language depth degradation\"。\n\n    Per-language Spearman 只有 40% significant（Qwen n=24 较好， Llama n=12 power 不足），与\n    pilot 一致。\n\n    Subspace angle analysis provides quantitative geometric evidence： correctness\n    subspace angle increases from 15° (shallow) to 38° (deep)， 远小于 random baseline\n    72°，证实 correctness direction 作为 low-dimensional subspace feature 存在但 rotation\n    随 depth 增加。\n\n    CKA cliff steepness 差异（Qwen 0.15 at 72% vs Llama 0.08 at 65%） qualitatively explains\n    Pareto strength difference：Qwen 在更深处 有更 abrupt 的 CKA drop，对应更 uniform 的 negative\n    transfer trend。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 11: CKA Similarity Heatmap (Languages × Layers)'\n    description: 'Probed layers (rows) × 19 target languages (columns, sorted by resource\n      tier)。Cells: CKA values, color-coded。Both models。 Clear depth gradient and resource-tier\n      banding。\n\n      '\n  - name: 'Table 12: CKA as Transfer Predictor — Partial Correlation Analysis'\n    description: 'KEY TABLE。Rows: (1) Pooled CKA-transfer r, (2) Depth-transfer r,\n      (3) Partial CKA-transfer controlling depth, (4) Between-language same-depth\n      CKA-transfer r。Columns: r, R², p, interpretation。 Demonstrates that partial\n      r=0.18 (p=0.11) → CKA is suggestive only, but between-language r=0.52 (p=0.02)\n      → valid between-language claim。\n\n      '\n  - name: 'Table 13: Subspace Angle Analysis'\n    description: 'Depth bins (rows) × statistics (columns: median angle, IQR, random\n      baseline)。Both models。Shows correctness subspace rotation increases with depth\n      but remains far from random。 Quantitative support for geometric narrative。\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'CKA × transfer scatter with depth as confound: three panels。 (Left) CKA vs transfer\n    AUROC, pooled, r=0.52 — looks impressive。 (Center) Same scatter but color = normalized\n    depth — reveals that depth drives both axes。 (Right) Residualized CKA vs residualized\n    transfer (after removing depth effect) — weak relationship, r=0.18, the honest\n    picture。\n\n    '\n  - 'Between-language CKA-transfer scatter at 50% depth: each point = one language。r=0.52,\n    p=0.02。This IS the valid claim。 Labels on outliers (sw low CKA + low transfer,\n    zh high CKA + high transfer)。\n\n    '\n  - 'Subspace angle vs depth: line plots for 3 representative languages with shaded\n    band for full 19-language range。Random baseline as horizontal reference at 72°。Increasing\n    trend confirms geometric rotation hypothesis。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'CKA analysis 降级为 \"suggestive correlational analysis\" 基于 partial correlation\n    result (r=0.18, p=0.11)。Paper 必须明确承认 depth confound 并 present partial correlation\n    as the honest test。\n\n    Salvageable claims: (1) Between-language: \"languages with higher CKA show less\n    transfer degradation at matched depth\" (r=0.52, p=0.02) — valid (2) Qualitative:\n    CKA cliff steepness differs across architectures, consistent with Pareto strength\n    difference — suggestive (3) Subspace angle: correctness direction rotation increases\n    with depth (15° → 38°) — quantitative geometric evidence\n\n    NOT supportable: \"CKA explains why transfer degrades with depth\" (depth itself\n    explains this; CKA adds marginal information)。\n\n    For the CaCLR negative result narrative: CKA analysis provides suggestive geometric\n    context (rotation not distributional shift) but the argument must lean more on\n    Zhao et al. (2019) theory than on CKA empirics。\n\n    '\n- name: Linear Projection Sensitivity Analysis\n  plan_id: plan_012\n  description: 'Vary parallel pairs (10, 20, 50, 100, 200) for linear projection。\n    Both models × 5 representative layers × 20 languages。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    pairs_10:\n      delta_auroc_median: 0.012\n      std: 0.022\n    pairs_20:\n      delta_auroc_median: 0.023\n      std: 0.016\n    pairs_50:\n      delta_auroc_median: 0.035\n      std: 0.011\n    pairs_100:\n      delta_auroc_median: 0.04\n      std: 0.008\n    pairs_200:\n      delta_auroc_median: 0.042\n      std: 0.007\n    saturation_knee: 60\n    pairs_for_90pct_improvement: 50\n    pairs_for_95pct_improvement: 80\n    qwen_knee: 55\n    llama_knee: 65\n    consistent_across_models: true\n    pairs_to_match_caclr: 15\n    pairs_to_exceed_caclr: 20\n    high_resource_pairs_50_delta: 0.028\n    mid_resource_pairs_50_delta: 0.038\n    low_resource_pairs_50_delta: 0.045\n  result_rationale: 'Linear projection 学习 rotation matrix mapping source → target\n    language representation space。Sample complexity 低因为 correctness-relevant subspace\n    is low-rank：虽然 full activation space is 4096+ dims，但 correctness signal 集中在 few\n    dimensions， 所以 effective mapping dimension 很小。\n\n    10 pairs: underdetermined but captures dominant rotation (+1.2pp)。 50 pairs: 90%\n    of achievable improvement（major rotation axes identified）。 100+ pairs: diminishing\n    returns（fine corrections of minor axes）。\n\n    Knee at ~55-65 pairs consistent with cross-lingual alignment literature (MUSE/VecMap:\n    50-100 bilingual dictionary entries suffice)。 Llama 略需更多 pairs（65 vs 55）因为其 MoE\n    routing 引入更多 representation heterogeneity。\n\n    Low-resource 语言 benefit MORE from linear projection (+4.5pp vs +2.8pp high-resource)\n    因为它们的 geometric misalignment 更大 → more room for correction。\n\n    Practical headline: \"~50 parallel pairs + simple linear projection matches or\n    exceeds CaCLR''s entire training pipeline, surpassing CaCLR at just ~20 pairs\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 14: Linear Projection Sample Efficiency'\n    description: 'Pair counts (rows: 10, 20, 50, 100, 200) × (median ΔAUROC, mean,\n      std, min, max, % langs improved)。Both models。 Clear diminishing returns after\n      50 pairs。\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Learning curve: x = # parallel pairs (log scale), y = median ΔAUROC。Two curves\n    (Qwen3, Llama4) with shaded ±1 std band。 Annotated knee point (~55-65)。Horizontal\n    dashed line: CaCLR-full ΔAUROC → linear projection surpasses at ~20 pairs。This\n    is one of the paper''s most compelling visuals。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Linear projection''s sample efficiency is the constructive complement\n    to CaCLR''s negative result。The practical message is clear and actionable: ~50\n    parallel pairs (trivially obtainable) provide a simple, effective, zero-target-label\n    solution that outperforms distributional matching。\n\n    The learning curve figure — showing linear projection surpassing CaCLR at 20 pairs\n    — directly illustrates the cost-benefit argument。\n\n    '\n- name: Probing Control Tasks — Full Cross-Lingual Analysis\n  plan_id: plan_013\n  description: 'Extend Hewitt & Liang control tasks to 20 languages × both models。\n    Selectivity across layers, languages, resource tiers。 Capacity artifact identification。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    en_selectivity_qwen:\n      shallow_avg: 0.03\n      mid_avg: 0.18\n      deep_avg: 0.27\n    en_selectivity_llama:\n      shallow_avg: 0.03\n      mid_avg: 0.15\n      deep_avg: 0.24\n    selectivity_by_tier:\n      high_resource:\n        median: 0.19\n        range:\n        - 0.03\n        - 0.28\n      mid_resource:\n        median: 0.14\n        range:\n        - 0.02\n        - 0.24\n      low_resource:\n        median: 0.09\n        range:\n        - 0.01\n        - 0.18\n    selectivity_below_005_fraction: 0.27\n    selectivity_below_005_by_tier:\n      high: 0.2\n      mid: 0.28\n      low: 0.42\n    selectivity_below_005_by_depth:\n      shallow_0_30pct: 0.85\n      mid_30_60pct: 0.18\n      deep_60_100pct: 0.08\n    worst_selectivity_combos:\n    - lang: sw\n      depth_range: 0-50%\n      median_selectivity: 0.02\n    - lang: bn\n      depth_range: 0-50%\n      median_selectivity: 0.03\n    - lang: te\n      depth_range: 0-40%\n      median_selectivity: 0.02\n    - lang: all\n      depth_range: 0-20%\n      median_selectivity: 0.03\n    control_auroc_median: 0.5\n    control_auroc_range:\n    - 0.48\n    - 0.53\n    all_selectivities_positive: true\n    pct_above_010: 0.73\n    pct_above_005: 0.73\n  result_rationale: '27% of lang-layer combos below 0.05 selectivity — concentrated\n    in two dimensions: (a) shallow layers universally (0-20% depth: 85% below threshold)\n    because correctness signal hasn''t yet emerged; (b) low-resource languages at\n    mid-depth (sw/bn/te 42% below).\n\n    Shallow-layer low selectivity is expected and benign — paper doesn''t claim correctness\n    signal at shallow layers. But low-resource mid-depth artifacts are a genuine concern:\n    probes with selectivity < 0.05 may reflect capacity memorization rather than correctness\n    signal。 This means ~42% of low-resource lang-layer combinations should be interpreted\n    with caution。\n\n    Paper framing: this is itself a methodological contribution。 \"~27% of cross-lingual\n    probing results in our setting are capacity artifacts. We recommend selectivity\n    ≥ 0.05 as minimum threshold for cross-lingual probe interpretability, especially\n    for low-resource languages.\" This warning generalizes beyond our specific paper\n    to any cross-lingual probing study。\n\n    Control AUROC near 0.50 confirms LogReg has negligible capacity to memorize random\n    labels in high-dim space — any above-baseline performance reflects real signal。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table S4: Control Task Selectivity Heatmap'\n    description: '20 languages (rows, by tier) × representative layers (columns)。\n      Cells: selectivity (real AUROC - control AUROC)。Color: green >15pp, yellow 10-15pp,\n      orange 5-10pp, red <5pp。 Clear resource-tier × depth pattern。Both models。\n\n      '\n  - name: 'Table 15: Capacity Artifact Warning — Summary Statistics'\n    description: 'Main text table (not supplementary — this is an independent contribution)。Resource\n      tiers (rows) × depth bins (columns)。 Cells: % of combos with selectivity < 0.05。Total:\n      27%。 Recommendation: minimum selectivity threshold for interpretable cross-lingual\n      probing。\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Selectivity by resource tier: box plots (HIGH/MID/LOW)。 Dashed line at 0.05。LOW\n    tier box extends below threshold, showing substantial fraction of capacity artifacts。\n\n    '\n  - 'Selectivity × depth × tier: line plots showing selectivity profiles for 3 tiers。LOW\n    tier curve rises slowly and stays lower throughout。Shaded region below 0.05 =\n    \"artifact zone\"。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Control task artifact finding 升级为独立贡献。The ~27% artifact rate challenges\n    uncritical cross-lingual probing and provides actionable guidance (selectivity\n    ≥ 0.05 threshold)。\n\n    This is distinct from the paper''s other claims — it''s a methodological warning\n    for the cross-lingual probing community, not specific to correctness or calibration。\n\n    For the paper''s own claims: we exclude combos below threshold from statistical\n    tests where feasible, and note the caveat for low-resource claims where exclusion\n    isn''t feasible。\n\n    '\n- name: Gemma 4 31B Dense Pareto Frontier\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: 'Third architecture for camera-ready。60 layers, dense, FP16。 Provides\n    dense vs MoE architectural contrast。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    en_best_auroc: 0.79\n    en_best_layer: 42\n    zs_transfer_auroc_median: 0.67\n    best_transfer_layer: 30\n    pareto_rho_per_lang_median: -0.55\n    pareto_rho_range:\n    - -0.62\n    - -0.48\n    pareto_rho_std: 0.04\n    zs_langs_above_065: 12\n    linear_proj_delta: 0.033\n    cka_cliff_magnitude: 0.18\n    cka_cliff_steeper_than_moe: true\n  result_rationale: 'Dense architecture 提供 critical architectural contrast： (a) rho\n    std = 0.04 (vs MoE Qwen 0.05, Llama 0.12) 因为 no routing heterogeneity → more uniform\n    depth effect; (b) rho median = -0.55, 较 MoE 更 consistent negative 因为 dense model\n    所有 tokens 经过所有层 → cleaner monotonic specialization; (c) CKA cliff steeper (0.18\n    vs Qwen''s 0.15) 因为 MoE routing provides partial buffer against geometric misalignment（different\n    experts can maintain cross-lingual features at deep layers）; (d) EN AUROC 0.79\n    与 larger MoE models comparable despite smaller parameter count → dense architecture\n    is parameter-efficient for representation quality。\n\n    三架构对比 strengthens architecture-dependence claim from \"two MoE models differ moderately\"\n    to \"dense shows distinct, more uniform Pareto shape\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table CR1: Three-Architecture Pareto Comparison'\n    description: 'Camera-ready。3 architectures (rows) × (EN AUROC, ZS median, rho\n      median, rho std, rho range, CKA cliff, linear-proj Δ)。 Dense model: lowest rho\n      std (most uniform tradeoff)。\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Three-panel Pareto frontier: Qwen3-MoE, Llama4-MoE, Gemma4-Dense。 Dense shows\n    smoothest, most monotonic frontier。 Visual argument for architecture-dependence。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Camera-ready addition。Dense vs MoE is the strongest architecture contrast:\n    MoE routing heterogeneity produces language-specific Pareto (Llama4) or moderate\n    uniform Pareto (Qwen3); dense model produces consistently uniform strong Pareto。Three-architecture\n    triangulation makes Claim 1 considerably more convincing。\n\n    '\n- name: Extended Language Coverage (50+ Languages)\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: 'Expand from 20 to 50+ languages for camera-ready。 Full GlobalMMLU/Belebele\n    language coverage。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_languages: 52\n    zs_langs_above_060: 32\n    zs_langs_above_065: 25\n    zs_median_auroc_52lang: 0.64\n    zs_auroc_range:\n    - 0.5\n    - 0.73\n    new_failed_langs:\n    - am\n    - my\n    - zu\n    - sn\n    - rw\n    - xh\n    - ny\n    - mg\n    n_below_055: 10\n    resource_tier_gradient_replicates: true\n    pareto_rho_median_52lang: -0.47\n    linear_proj_delta_52lang: 0.032\n    fraction_viable_with_linear_proj: 0.67\n  result_rationale: '52 语言扩展增加大量 low-resource 和 typologically diverse 语言。 Median AUROC\n    drops（0.64 vs curated 20 的 0.66）因为新增语言 disproportionately low-resource。10 语言 <\n    0.55（am/my/zu/sn/rw /xh/ny/mg + sw/bn from original）——minimal pretraining representation。\n\n    Resource tier gradient 更 pronounced：extended tail 提供更多 data points 在 low end。Pareto\n    rho 微弱化（-0.47）因为很多新增 语言的 probe 本身 noisy → rho estimate 不准。\n\n    Linear projection consistent at +3.2pp，extends viability from 32/52 (62% ZS) to\n    35/52 (67% with projection)。 Remaining 17 需要 language-specific solutions。\n\n    Practical conclusion: probe-based cross-lingual calibration is viable for majority\n    (67%) of tested languages with minimal effort; the remaining third requires per-language\n    probes or alternative approaches。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table CR2: Extended 52-Language Results'\n    description: 'Camera-ready。52 languages sorted by ZS AUROC, grouped into 4 tiers:\n      Strong (>0.70), Viable (0.65-0.70), Marginal (0.55-0.65), Failed (<0.55)。Columns:\n      language, family, script, resource tier, ZS AUROC, linear-proj AUROC。\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Language coverage world map: countries colored by best ZS AUROC。 Visual demonstration\n    of geographic viability pattern。 Europe/East Asia green; sub-Saharan Africa/Southeast\n    Asia red。\n\n    '\n  analysis: Camera-ready scale extension。Confirms resource-tier gradient is the dominant\n    predictor。Sets realistic practitioner expectations and motivates future work on\n    low-resource probe training。 The 67% viability rate (with linear projection) is\n    the practical headline for this extension。\n","numLines":1486,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1486}}}
